{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay","id":1551806,"title":"Ideas for Fan Exalted types - Yay or nay?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-21T11:35:22-07:00","id":1551806,"title":"Ideas for Fan Exalted types - Yay or nay?","content":"So I have several ideas for new Exalted types and while I never developed them too much I would like to see if people think there is any potential for them; also all names are place holder at the current point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Abstruse/Xana/Xeno<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> If Sidereals are IT specialists and Getimeans are hackers, than these guys are the weirdoes who think we went the wrong path with transistors and are trying to build vacuum tubes out of living matter. Abstruse Exalts wield powers that bend not what reality can be but what it should be and often invoke otherworldly forces in their charms (like psychic gases, radioactive material and the like).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> Xana/Norns - a collection of ancient potential incarnae abandoned and sealed by the Primordials at the dawn of Creation as being unnecessary. Recently released they have made their own Exalted to try and find a place in the world/claim it for the Primordials.<br /> <br /> Probably named after dwarf planets (like Orcus, Sedna, Gongong, etc) or alternative names for the major planets (like Stilbon for Mercury or Nergal for Mars). Most likely potential maidens of fate or a balancing group abandoned for not being useful (Norns); their domains might be Hospitality, Labour, Harmony, Savagery and Beginnings (opposed to Journeys, Serenity, Battles, Secrets and Endings respectively) another idea was elemental dragons of elements abandoned at the design floor due to being impractical, too odd or dangerous, like a version of radiactive metals or a self replicating crystal like tiberium from the Command and Conquer series (Xana). Possible a combination of the two.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> If the Norn then Hospitality, Labour, Harmony, Savagery and Beginnings with either planets symbols if their patrons are named as dwarf planets or set of three line ( forming a triangle for Hospitality, on stack atop of each for labour, don\u2019t know for Harmony, three lines stack diagonally for Savagry and three lines from a central point). Don\u2019t know what it would if it\u2019s Xana patrons, but definitely based on weird/unused potential elements.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Past, Regret, things that are not of this world (like alien substances, impossible creatures, weird laws of physics), Change, Potential, Regression.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Sidereal; only about 100 in existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> People who had greatest denied by their own choices<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> I original came up with idea as part of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1548099-concept-for-alternative-infernal-origins#post1551601\">this post</a> on an alternative Infernals origins and I don't know if they can stand up on their own. I also have no cool 'secondary' power for them (like Sidereal's writing of fate or Lunar Shapeshifting; the best I could think of was some sort of meddling with the past but I don't think stepping on the some of the fundamental rules of Exalted and also if I did something like that, Temporals would make the best option for it). The name \u2018Abstruse\u2019 I choose not only as an alternative to \u2018arcane\u2019, \u2018obscure\u2019 or \u2018occult\u2019 in meaning but also to be, well, obscure to most people.<br /> <br /> ____________________________<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Angelic/Virtuous Exalted<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Exalted is about Great People, not Good People; Angelic exalted are specifically in defiance of that; they are chosen to represent and encourage certain virtues while driving back moral failure. While not under the Great Curse, they similarly suffer under the burden of having to embody their virtue or else experience massive manic periods of it; also they can temporarily absorb the Great Curse from other Exalted but suffer from it\u2019s effects instead. Angelics might be the embodiments of specific virtues, but due to how they exalt, they\u2019re often people who originally didn\u2019t live up to those ideals and now have to learn to do so. Their charms would be supportive and empowering but lack ways to directly hurt others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> Elpis was not only a proto-type of the later deities but specifically of what would become the Unconquered Sun. However the Primordials quickly learned of a fault in this design; while Elpis would be the embodiment of that was good the Ebon Dragon wanted to oppose, he was tied more closely to the nature of reality than later Gods and more like one of the Primordials \u2013 if Elpis came into being then his high moral values would warp the Primordials \u2013 as such they quickly bound him to a dungeon beyond reality and paved over the door with a layer of existence.<br /> <br /> Elpis would have stayed there had not the Primordial War occurred (which ironically might not have happened had they taken Elpis\u2019 presence and become more compassionate), and the destruction of vast swathes of Creation lead to Elpis\u2019 mausoleum. Fighting through the various behemoths and living shadows, the Exalted explorers found the half finished proto-incarnae and offered to take him to Yu Shan. However removing the seal of that wretched place removed the existential pressure on Elpis, so he faded away only whispering about something of having to fix a curse.<br /> <br /> Centuries later, the first Angelics appeared, many knowing this story innately and seeking to stop the excesses the Solars \u2013 unfortunately the initial encounters often lead to the death of the Angelics and was another tick for the Sidereals to launch the Usurpation, which could have been stopped if the Angelics could have succeeded.<br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Based off of various virtues, probably the 4 Virtues of prior editions plus either Hope or Truth. Might be solely based off western angels but could have castes based on other angelic beings from mythology like Valkyries or Tennin, or one a set of legendary beasts based on behemoths from Elpis\u2019 dungeon that were convinced by the mutterings of his ideas like phoenixes, kirins, etc.<br /> <br /> Either way their anima barriers only appear as wings that allow them to fly (although the patterns and colours of the wings depend on each exalt; might also have sound based aspects to the anima (like a celestial choir). If using the other angelic being inspiration certain castes have different animas (like multiples arms) but all of them would have tangible effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Virtue, light, second chances, rebirth, flight, Irony, justice, zealotry, hope, healing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Probably Celestial, maybe Solar. 50-100 in number.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> All Angelic start off as someone who is close to greatness but only limited by a vice; in a moment of reaching to a certain virtue allows them to exalt. A dark variant is that Elpis didn\u2019t have enough strength to make the Exaltation and thus for each exaltation a sacrifice must be made \u2013 Angelic exaltations occur when someone makes a big enough sacrifice that it draws the potential exaltation to them and completely consumes them to fuel the Exaltation before choosing the nearest person who would benefit from the virtue of the most in the nearby area.<br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> While an interesting concept, and I one I like, I feel it would be too easy to fumble this one.<br /> <br /> ________<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Chaotic/Xaotic<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Chosen of manifold chaos of the Wyld, Chaotics are mad revolutionaries. While they draw on Wyld for power, they have little association with Fair Folk directly and are instead the champions of chaos itself; their powers are about sowing chaos and transformation rather than the stories and many Chaotic find themselves neither in home amongst the Creationborn or with the Fair Folk. Do not suffer from the Great Curse but do go insane from time to time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> None; their exaltation was created by a host of Fair Folk caught in the Scarlet Empresses counter attack to the Balor Crusade; as Creation reasserted itself and crushed this army, it\u2019s leader (a particular old Fair Folk who helped in the Primordial War but had become bitter at the rule of the Exalted didn\u2019t undo 100% of the Primordial\u2019s work) sacrificed not only himself but his entire army to create Exaltations to get vengeance on all Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Not fully sure, first idea was to have them based on opposing aspects of Creation that are anti-thetical to pure chaos (like time, space, mtter, etc) or how their Exaltation immediately affected their life (ruining it, making people afraid of them, liberation, etc) or a set of completely random concepts (Like the colour Orange, the number Pi, Left handiness, etc). Caste marks look like a random splatter pattern with the caste symbol as a cut out in the middle. Might also change castes every now and again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Chaos, madness, change, freedom, rebellion, luck, foolishness, the Wyld, mutation, outsiders, social exclusion, societal collapse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Celestial, couple of hundred in number.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> Either it\u2019s 100% random or whoever\u2019s exaltation will cause the a decent amount of chaos at the point of Exaltation in a radius of roughly 100 miles of a Chaotic exalt dying.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> While I like the basic concept, it seems too wishy-washy to be viable and Dream Souled seem to take a lot of the same idea space to stand out.<br /> <br /> ___________________<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Dichotomal<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Chosen of dualities, Dichotomals are always seeking and causing conflicts and compromises as live. Each one was originally two people who were fused into one and fight to control how their new life goes \u2013 Gesalt is used to describe the individual made by this fusion and interplay of competing personalities.. Additionally each Exalt pair has a chosen \u2018Nemesis\u2019, a person (usually another Exalt) they are supposed to face down and challenge as part of their new hybrid nature. Some of their abilities work better on the Nemesis and they also always know where their nemesis is at any time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> Janus, the Incarnae of Duality who serves to ensure balance and independence existed between the Primordials\u2019 Creations. He was prone to inciting violence amongst others in the pursuit of competition, Janus was however a fair judge as he always listened and contemplated both sides. Currently split in half and imprisoned in both Yu-Shan and Malfeas after fighting on both sides of the Primordial War and his host had similarly been split in two during the war leading to their imprisonment. It was thought his Exaltations were stretched out between the two locations and thus couldn\u2019t Exalt, but since the mid Shogunate Dichotomals have returned to the confusion of everyone involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Not sure, but likely based on pairs of opposing concepts like War-Peace or Love-Hate; either that or different kinds of relationships with each half getting a different caste and the Gesalt swaps between them as one personality becomes stronger or weaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Duality, Rivalry, conflict, marriage, relationships of all kinds, trade, mirrors, reflections, extremes, compromises, alternative viewpoints, challenge, doubt, co-operation, balance, judgment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Celestial \u2013 roughly 200 in number.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> Two very different people who cross paths \u2013 if their combined potential is greater than the sum of their parts they will merge them into a new Dichotomal Exalt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> Too mechanically clunky for it\u2019s own good, and the optional Umbrals also do the whole traitorous incarnate and competing personality so I should probably bin this idea; however the Nemesis system could work elsewhere.<br /> <br /> ________________________<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Industrial<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Empowered by the scientific principles of a strange world in an alternative universe called \u2018Earth\u2019; Industrials were created when Autochthon attempted to make a bridge to this world but didn\u2019t work until he had sent himself to elsewhere and the Seal of Eight Divinities was cracked open allowing the Industrial Exaltations to exist. In addition to their science based powers, Industrials are the best at using the new three way portal system that exists between Earth, Autocthonia and Creation. See more details here (Insert Industrials Link).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> Technically Autocthon, but Industrials have little connection to him at this point. Could possibly have a bunch of scientists develop the power of the Exaltations beyond their initial seed but that feels a little weird.<br /> <br /> <b>Castes: </b><br /> <br /> Each Exalt has an aspect (bases on the Autochthonian elements) and a Caste (Based on various sciences). Castes marks are triangular in shape and instead of having regular Anima barriers their Animas manifest as mechanic power armour that can upgraded s they strong<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Science, discovery, reason, elements of autochthon, research, upgrading, progress, civilization, forces of nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Celestial, roughly 300 in number.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> Someone who takes action when someone else fails to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> I love these guys - but they\u2019re a disjointed mess that would need a lot of work to even make right (see some of my original ideas <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/25328-industrial-exalted-the-twin-chosen-bastards-of-autochthon-fan-splat/page2\">here</a>). The basic concept alone is a mess (science based exalts with a tie to our Earth and Autochthon) and if I ever did work on this I think I would need to rebuild it from the ground up (probably dropping the major Autochthon elements and focusing on the version of Earth present and the science themes \u2013 which in turn has it\u2019s own problems (Current the plot is Earth link to Creation somehow (possibly Bridge to Nowhere) -&gt; Scientist discover miracle of Exaltat -&gt; ???? -&gt; Make Exaltations -&gt; Open portals to Creation).), and that's considering they were very much a 2nd edition idea when I had them.<br /> <br /> ___________________________________<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Plague<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Survivors of a mystical plague that kills most of it\u2019s victims, the survivors become agents of this plague, gaining access to it\u2019s sickening powers and joining it\u2019s community of fellow exalts. Plague exalted are weaker than most exalts but are natural drawn to each allowing them to find community and support. They find it hard to interact with mortals due their charms and anima barriers spread their infection; the Infection is persistent, killing most hosts but sparing a few as new exalts. Plague exalts have powers of sickening and weakening targets to more easily overwhelm them with numbers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> The originator the Infection is unknown; whether a Primordial weapon, the exigence of a plague or a Fair Folk joke, but it has since spread beyond the control of anyone. The plague now spreads on it\u2019s own, killing some victims and using their deaths as fuel for new exaltations; while it has no central intelligence it does have some sort of presence in the minds of the Plague exalted, but whether these are the whispers of a patron, the collective voice of a subconscious hive mind or just the accumulated knowledge of their fellow exalts is unknown and still debated on by scholars. It\u2019s history is dated to at least the mid-First Age and several times the disease has been virtually eliminated only to return years later through various mechanisms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Either various vectors of infection (for example air borne, animal bites, etc) or different strands of the Infection the have evolved over time, meaning historically their castes are quite different. Anima Barriers tend to be a sickly green mixed with purple.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Disease, sickness, erosion, corruption, mutation, evolution, spreading, expansion, growth, decay<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Terrestrial, numbers recorded between 0 and 5000 at various points of history.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> When the Infection takes hold in someone it will lead to 1 of 4 ends: near immediate death of the host, which uses their life force and sometimes even their soul to fuel the next two possibility; exaltation if enough life force has been extracted in other nearby victims; asymptomatic exaltation where the new exalt won\u2019t manifest powers for months or even uses before randomly exalting one day, during this whole time they spread the Infection subtly and it reawakens at their exaltation; or unexalted asymptomatic carriers who also spread the Infection secretly (and often without their knowledge) until such point the Infection reclaims their body and they face either of the previous 3 options. No mortal has ever been known to survive the infection uninfected without supernatural aid from Exalts.<br /> <br /> Additionally, through charms, random chance in the infection cycle or actively certain strains during an unexalted asymptomatic\u2019s life, the host\u2019s very soul is tainted by the Infection; it does not reincarnate as normal but remains a sickly ghost until it naturally reincarnates into a child that would be otherwise stillborn \u2013 the infection then re-emerges during their teens or twenty starting a new outbreak. This along with tainted items has allow the Infection to survive 3 successful attempts to purge the disease in the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> While a fun idea, I\u2019m worried they might become a little too antagonist (what with the spreading sickness everywhere and the tendency to form communities of survivor Exalts after the loss of whole communities) to be good player options.<br /> <br /> _______________________<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Prehuman/Shedim/Denisovan/Xenos<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Chosen of Several pre-human races that sacrificed their existences to create a new breed of Exalts to over throw the Solars and the Incarnae. Most of the powers would involve either warping their bodies or replicating the powers of those lost species. Might have abilities to pass on their traits to followers and half-castes but still not sure. Would also be drawn to others of their kind and reshaping humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> A collection of pre-human species that gave up their collective existences to empower humans to great revenge at the Incarnae and the Solar aligned exalted. Currently have no overseeing god or demon over sees them. Not sure what exactly their patron races were like but mostly weird inhuman things straight out of the Cthulhu Mythos or other strange fantasy/sci-fi settings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Based on the various species; might also have a caste/aspect system from the Industrial Exalt idea with aspects being the patron race and caste is the role expected of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Other than revenge, community and strange biology, I\u2019m not sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Celestial, roughly 200 to 300 in strength<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> Not sure, might differ from Caste to caste.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> Currently only a framework now, and quite tied to this alternative ideas for Infernals (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1548099-concept-for-alternative-infernal-origins#post1551601\">see this link</a>) as secondary exalted; not sure what else to do with them or if they are worth any thought. Differ from the Spoken of the Niobrarans by being humans empowered rather than some non-human race.<br /> <br /> _________________________<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Primordial/Emergent<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Humans given power by mysterious patron causing their souls to emerge as two pseudo-deva/demons called Peri. Primordial Exalted can either have their Peri as independent beings out in the world or residing within themselves, with the ability to swap in and out with a minor ceremony; while out in the world the Peri acts as an independent being but while within their Exalt the Exalt can use the Peri\u2019s powers as their own. Without their Peri the Primordial Exalt is fairly weak with only few charm options.<br /> <br /> If a Peri is downed without a spirit killing magical effect it will reform over several weeks to months within their Exalt, during which time the Exalt will be weakened; if a spirit killing effect is used on the Peri, then their Exalt will automatically die. If the Exalt dies but both Peri are alive, they have a year and day to find a way to resurrect the Exalt before the exaltation leaves and they must become regular souls again in Lethe \u2013 if one is downed then the other Peri has a month and day to find a way to resurrect the Exalt \u2013 what this entails is on a case by case basis but usually involves fixing the body of whatever damage it took and get life giving essence of some sort within it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> Seventh Soulless \u2013 a mysterious being who claims to be the god of the concept of Primordials, but he\u2019s exact nature is uncertain. Some think him an escape demon, powerful Fair Folk or something without a legitimate known category but whatever the details, he is relative obscure beyond his champions but seems friendly to those who approach him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Not sure but each Exalt likely has two; one for the Po Peri and one for the Hun Peri to make desigining them easier; whether these are in universe concepts or just design templates for pcs I don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Not sure, but likely souls and questions of identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Solar with their two Peri in place, low celestial with on in their soul and low terrestrial with both Peri out. The Peri would be roughly low celestial in power level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> Not Sure<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> Originally an Exigent concept, they have more going on so it might worth developing more. Little worried the Peri system might make them too powerful with them being effectively two extra bodies they can use.<br /> <br /> ______________________<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Supernal<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Basically toying with Primordial being defined by one of their charms and what happens if a mortal learns one of them. That kinda evolved into an Exalted type where one Primordial gave their charms to Mortals at some point and their various Deva took part of their patron\u2019s power to allow these mortal to use these charms as Exalts and not just be driven mad/mutated.<br /> <br /> Each one has only one Primordial charm, as any more would be too much for the Exalt but each charm is major power in itself (like turning a target into a minor copy of the Unconquered Sun for essence rounds or magical inserting a law (natural or legal) on a region for a year and a day). Also pros at sorcery and Necormancy (able to learn both to the highest level simultaneously breaking the usual ways), otherwise very weak (the idea being a seemingly weaker member of the party who can unleash immense power in specific situations).<br /> <br /> Also they would all have Occult as a favourite ability like third edition Sidereals and Martial Arts<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> Arcanus \u2013 a primordial of uncertain domain who is the patron of Sorcery (although that\u2019s like say Gaia is the patron of rivers; technically derived from what she manages but not a core element of it). Asleep either before the Primordial war, his Deva made the Supernal Exalted by taking away his ability to awakening as part of the Law of Diminishment. Note his current fetch is actually an illusion of the original, and if ever dispelled or proven to be false, Arcanus will change as if through Fetch death; his actual fetch is now a hecatoncheire in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Based on the Primordial charm granted by their patron.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Raw Power, Miracles, Sorcery<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Solar Level Sorcery, Void Level Necromancy, one very powerful charm, dragon blood level in other stuff (or maybe even weaker than that).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> Not certain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique</b>:<br /> <br /> Fun little idea, but balancing how world breaking the Primordial Charms should be could be a little complicated. Original concept was for a sort of Akuma exalt for the Yozis before it became it\u2019s own thing.<br /> <br /> _____________________<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Temporal<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Time based exalts chosen by a missing patron, Temporals are exalts with immense but unusual powers. Some of the abilities include enhancing their speed, reducing the speeds of others, holding off damage to the future, increasing recovery rate, peering into the past and future, etc. Might have the ability to \u2018time travel\u2019 to a sort of enter a phantom-image of the past or future, with only the Present being \u2018real\u2019, anything taken from the past or future will cease to be and changes will be unimportant but it can be used to do things like travel on forgotten roads, locate lost objects, see where people run to, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> Either a pair of Incarnae (Chronos and Aion) or a weird Primordial of Time who is constantly switching places with their fetch soul in a cycle that powers the movement of time. In the Incarnae version had the Primordial create the Incarne of time, Chronos, but due to his constant pranks he was imprisoned and replaced with a more docile incarnate, Aion, who was a lot weaker. While Aion was not trusted by the other Incarnae, they did side with others in the Divine Revolution but stole most of Chronos\u2019 power to create the Temporal Exalted; however the Primordial released Chronos during the war and he dragged Aion and their Exalts into a war across time and space until they eventually made peace and have returned to the present with a tentative peace deal and a plan to share their office duties and time at the Games of Divinity to keep time moving.<br /> <br /> In the Primordial version, the original Titan of Time had two fetch souls (Chronos and Aion) that constantly fought for the role; this interplay kept the very flow of time moving. However the Titan of Time was eventual overthrown by his fetch souls with the help of the other Primordials as they feared the titan\u2019s bas concept \u2013 the new overcoming the old. Eventual the Chronos/Aion Primordial start espousing the same ideas as the old Primordial and thus they were sentenced to exile to the second before the present. The Aion/Chronos primordial is thus stuck in the past and relies on their exalted as agents in the present.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Either three; Past, Present and Future based on personal values and general approach to life (past are historians and traditionalists, present are daredevils and the quick witted while future are planners and schemers) or time scales (such as Seconds, Minutes, Hours, etc, that based on what sort of role is expected of the Exalt). Caste marks appear as a pale beige in colour and the light is less intense that Solar or Lunar animas<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Time, preservation, future, past, preparation, quickness, speed, slowness, foresight, retrocognition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power Level:</b><br /> <br /> Celestial, 100-200<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Traits looked for in an Exalt:</b><br /> <br /> Not sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Personal Critique:</b><br /> <br /> While there is an obvious thematic gap that a time based exalt could fit in, I\u2019m not sure of a second power that doesn\u2019t become broken.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: fixing hyperlinks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":1291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","user":"Mr.Jaxus","date":". 06-21-2025, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T05:05:30-07:00","id":1552363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay#post1551806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have several ideas for new Exalted types and while I never developed them too much I would like to see if people think there is any potential for them; also all names are place holder at the current point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope you don't mind me saying, but it kind of feels like you are really hang up in &quot;make a big, bad, celestial exalt type&quot; high concept, what kind of creates its own hurdles and then throwing ideas on a wall to see if you get something to stick. Kind of scattershot, specially with everything put together like that with the thematic zig-zag that reading through them all kind of produces in one's head. Seems like you're kind of setting yourself up for getting lost and burned out like that.<br /> <br /> Not blaming you, everybody has probably at some time or other toyed with the idea of making a new type of exalt of their own, but that Nocturnals is the big deal it is goes to show how crazy challenging making it happen can be.<br /> <br /> So i'd say - focus on finding a solid idea to expand upon - like, Liminals being patchwork-people made from multiple corpses and fragments of the memories of the dead imbued into those parts, trying to develop an identity that goes beyond the haphazard sum of its parts through interaction and protection of the living &amp;/or the dead, for example - that opens room for some peculiar roleplaying and mechanic gimmicks of their own.<br /> <br /> Liminals in fact make a great example of how a new exalt can have A LOT in common with a more established one - it's hilariously easy to just peg them as &quot;abyssals-lite&quot; or &quot;CotD's Prometheans adapted to Exalted&quot; - but at the same time the idea behind them has more than enough heft to work from to make their lore, aims and the experience of playing one, from roleplaying and mechanic perspectives both, quite different in many ways.<br /> <br /> Liminals power level? Supposedly terrestrial-ish, if memory tricks me not; Total numbers? Damned if i know, if any was ever given (Not to mention Sovereigns can be seen as pretty much an official example of a concept finding an unique way to cheat with the matter of numbers).<br /> <br /> <br /> So my first suggestion is: take those two things - that also happen to be the most defined element across all your samples - leave them aside, they are arbitrary objectives that help nothing with developing a character and in fact can turn all too easily into hurdles. Same for castes, leave all of those for <b><i>after </i></b>you have some more solid imagery around a concept to get you going.<br /> <br /> <br /> Explore the basic concepts and the patrons, try to dive deeper into them, dig some cool imagery to build character concepts or gimmicks from. And it doesn't have to be something utterly different or unlike already existing mechanics - is Liminals acessing memories from the people whose parts are composed of SO different from Celestial exalts getting flashbacks from the lives of previous holders of their exaltation, or Dragon-Blooded getting memories or intimacies passed through the blood &amp; essence of their ancestors with Dynasty-keyword charms? It's all in finding the right twist, or combination of them, to make your Chosen shine.<br /> <br /> Speaking of twists and combinations, don't be affraid to cut, drop or re-stitch together the parts in novel, stranger ways. I can definitely see some common elements between &quot;Abstruse&quot;, &quot;Dichotomal&quot;, &quot;Emergent&quot; &amp; &quot;Temporal&quot; to blend into something greater than the sum of the parts perhaps.<br /> <br /> Does a certain concept really works to jumpstart an exalt-spirit-primordial race-etc or maybe it's better as some sort of piece of lore, crossover adventure or whole Shard instead? Industrials do give me that impression.<br /> Or does it offer ideas for a whole plethora of small tricks or a world-shaking one-trick pony? Supernals in particular come to mind, as your description of &quot;primordial powers&quot; makes me think more of &quot;i dropped a Sidereal MA post-Form charm or Adamant Circle spell into the hands of a rando&quot; more than anything like &quot;acessing a Primordial charm tree and evolving along with it as one's mastery of Essence grows&quot; as we see with Infernals.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts, feel free to agree or disagree, thrown some more details on whoever you feel like and whatever ideas or opinions my comments may elicit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-25-2026, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T02:27:19-07:00","id":1552406,"title":"","content":"Time to invest some jade where my mouth is as the saying goes, so let me tackle one of your kids.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay#post1551806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Name:</b><br /> <br /> Prehuman/Shedim/Denisovan/Xenos<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic Concept:</b><br /> <br /> Chosen of Several pre-human races that sacrificed their existences to create a new breed of Exalts to over throw the Solars and the Incarnae. Most of the powers would involve either warping their bodies or replicating the powers of those lost species. Might have abilities to pass on their traits to followers and half-castes but still not sure. Would also be drawn to others of their kind and reshaping humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Atavic/Atavistic</b> aka &quot;Cavemenxalted/Chosen of Fossils/Ressurectionists/Chimerae&quot;<br /> <br /> Easiest... name.... choice.... ever......<br /> Seriously, it's like their concept was tailor made for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atavism\" target=\"_blank\">this word</a>.<br /> <br /> Can definitely see those guys &amp; gals fitting in some funky peculiar niches of their own hidden in the conceptual space between Lunars, with the whole &quot;taking into the forms and qualities of other (once-)living creatures, sometimes creating populations of hybrids with humans as followers, when not remaking them wholesale&quot; theme, but also some of Abyssals, in that they focus on <b>dead </b>beings, extinct species whose hungry, angry &amp;/or plain eerie ghosts those chosen must appease, deal with, maybe reintegrate within the reincarnation cycle through the return of their kind?<br /> <br /> Also, completely apart of these, the &quot;people that hide within their bodies and souls supposedly long dead pre-human critters that orchestrate from the shadows a return to past glories&quot; is something with <b>a lot</b> of &quot;reptilian conspiracy&quot; vibes, what i find a quite interesting angle all of their own to mess with.<br /> <br /> (Some &quot;Shadow over Innsmouth&quot;-style ancestry/body horror potential mixed in too, for certain)<br /> <br /> <br /> Chimerae i added as a possible alternate name because it crossed my mind that dealing with urges, mindset and priorities of a alien dead backseat passenger in one's head could be hectic, to say the least. Add to that a inner library of multiple dead inhuman critters.... and one can see how the &quot;losing oneself between all the changes&quot; conceit behind 2e lunar chimeras might resonate to some degree with the Atavics, i think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay#post1551806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Patron:</b><br /> <br /> A collection of pre-human species that gave up their collective existences to empower humans to great revenge at the Incarnae and the Solar aligned exalted. Currently have no overseeing god or demon over sees them. Not sure what exactly their patron races were like but mostly weird inhuman things straight out of the Cthulhu Mythos or other strange fantasy/sci-fi settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively and to try to play in some of the theme-mingling with Lunars, their patron could be Gaia, one of her less-known Devas, the Animal Fathers/Mothers, or the eastern jungle goddess Arilak (that if memory tricks me not, had a strong connection with collecting animals of all sorts - <i>and kept a bunch of extinct beasts she was supposed to have eliminated millenia ago </i>still alive and healthy in secret reserves within her sanctum or somewhere else) for some quick, lore-friendly suggestions.<br /> <br /> [Personally, to mess around further with the &quot;dead things not quite as gone as expected trying to make a comeback&quot; angle, i'm tempted to suggest Moonshadow, the goddess of <b><i>lunar </i></b>eclipses no one talks about though it should - possibly an aspect of Luna that was lost/gained &quot;life&quot; of her own sometime between the first solar eclipse and the formation of the Underworld with the first Primordial death. Also messing around with the whole &quot;between lunars &amp; abyssals&quot; narrative space a bit]<br /> <br /> It all depends on how one wants to scale them in relation to other Exalted or what sounds more fun to expand upon, i guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT based on your initial idea of savant-sorcerers of Primordial races managing to implant a bunch of people with <i>something </i>that would make them into agents of their return on their own with no numimous help from high above/down below/sideways or whatever, i just remembered the Genesis Lords from DotFA, a group of people that managed to create a magical virus that will replicate the memories, personalities &amp; skills of individual savants of this civilization destroyed by the Exalted Host sometime a little after the Primordial War. So we have at least one solid canon example of a similar thing - that also crosses over with your &quot;Plague (Vector/vectorial?) exalted&quot; concept, so more than one path can be taken when it comes to patrons, power-scaling &amp; such.<br /> <br /> As an aside, if City Fathers &amp; Mothers can pool resources as a group to dilute the backlash of exigence and make their own brand of Chosen through this sort of rules-bending, why not disease gods, out of a &quot;neighborhood watch/peer aid fellowship&quot; arrangement to avoid another Contagion-level scenario or similar foul play from beings outside Creation with their domains?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay#post1551806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Castes:</b><br /> <br /> Based on the various species; might also have a caste/aspect system from the Industrial Exalt idea with aspects being the patron race and caste is the role expected of the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say various species of lost Primordial creations would be more like a Lunar's totem/spirit shape than Castes per se, but that's me nitpicking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay#post1551806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Themes:</b><br /> <br /> Other than revenge, community and strange biology, I\u2019m not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Memorializing, long lost lore, reconstruction, adapting past things to the present, struggling with urges &amp; interests of long-dead alien ghosts for good or for ill, speculative biology, history &amp; myths, historical revisionism, balancing the needs of those who exist in the past with realities of the present or future.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rough, bumpy and sketchy, but hopefully we can get a start out of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Extra - maybe it's my brain going on overdrive with drawing parallels between different things, but just crossed my mind that the &quot;kind of like Lunars but yet quite divergent in directions, goals &amp; themes&quot; deal these beings have going on for them could perhaps draw some ideas of the Okami from the Burn Legend shard back in late 2e, that while clearly meant as a Lunar expy also have some quite curious particularities and twists of their own. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-07-2025, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T03:44:23-07:00","id":1552695,"title":"","content":"So a couple of points.<br /> <br /> -If you're attempting a new Exalt type (as oppose to a once-and-done Exigent or a group of Exigents), I think one of the first questions you need to ask is what your Creation and your chronicle gains from there being that many of them and by extension how they conduct and organise themselves. <br /> <br /> -I remember many years ago Morke and Holden talking about caste/aspects in the context of homebrew Exalt types and saying how the percieved need to create a subcatagorisation can weaken a solid core concept, for example someone being a Chosen of Volcanoes is a cool idea but if you then feel they need 5 castes in order to be a &quot;real&quot; Exalt and this can either stretch the concept or use weak distinctions that makes the whole thing feel more contrived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T11:56:39-07:00","id":1552723,"title":"","content":"Well, of course you wouldn't have 5 divisions for volcanoes. There are three types of them, and one is a midway point between the other two, so either they have three aspects or they're like Getimians and switch between states.<br /> <br /> (aa and pahoehoe lava types probably work in differently...)<br /> <br /> [/at least somewhat missing the point]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T17:12:32-07:00","id":1553115,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a>, thanks for all that, I completely missed the name idea of Atavic/Atavistic exalted, and I thank you for all the ideas you put up for it. I was meaning to get back to this sooner but I kept being delayed so please don't hold it against me. If I do work on it do you mind if I take your ideas going forward? Espeically the concept of Moonshadow being their patron, I like that - gives the concept of a previously unknown incarnae without having to make up a load of stuff or justifying why they're only now appearing. Although if I remember correctly Luna was made by taking several potential Lunar gods and pitching them into fighting each other until only one crawled out, so maybe one or more of them survived and became the new patron(s) after escaping from Lunar for so long. Not 100% sold on mixing them with the Plague Exalted but I think that could be repurposed as lesser servants of the Atavic exalted, a sort of forerunner they release to break populations and push people into being worthy of the Atavic exaltation while weakening enemy resistance.<br /> <br /> I did have some thoughts since my first post, mostly because also I independently realised that merging some of concepts could work to make stronger ideas:<br /> <br /> * Temporals + Abstruse/Xana/Xeno + possibly Dichotimals + possibly Emergents + possibly Angelics + possibly Xeno; the idea was the Titan of Time's actually central concept was the line between Primordial and non-primordial; unfortunately some of his/her/their/it's ideas were horrid to the Primordials (like they should also die like lesser beings and be reincarnated), so they helped his/her/their/it's twin fetch's over throw him/her/them/it and alternate as Primordial and Fetch in an internal cycle that moves time forward; the five remaining souls (that didn't switch around between 3rd and 2nd level with each swapping of the primordial and fetch) became the Norns and sought some ways to test Primordials and Non-primordials, eventually sinking into a moment in the past to hide as they helped pushed the Primordial War and the rise of the Solars to see if they could test the line between Primordial and Non-primordial. Eventually the Norns made their own chosen to push the boundries and see if they can make things that challenge the lines set in sand by the Primordials (like the ban on time travel or raising the dead), with all Temporals being transgressors seeking to push various boundries. Castes would likely be based on what they're meant to challenge (like the other Exalted, the cycle of Reincarnation, Morality, Soul Structures, etc) with their time powers mostly used to protect them as they experiment. Emergent inspiration would be them developing soul structures like 2nd Edition Infernals; possibly Angelics and Xenos by having some of their castes focus on what it means to be of a particular species and what it means to embody a particular ideal to it's extremes. Dichotimal influnces would be present in how Norn's Primordial is in an internal conflict and a lot of their charms could have duality themes and focus on some nemesis or goal they have to challenge. But what ever I include I think I should focus on the Temporals + Abstruse/Xana/Xeno core and work from that.<br /> <br /> * Industrial + Prehuman/Shedim/Denisovan/Xenos: Basically the the Bridge to Nowhere created a mostly empty universe that became our one except several ancient alien species existed before us; what little of the Wyld's essence could seep in via the bridge became a drug/power up to them and they sought ways to extract more of it, however they were limited until humanity evolved and their sympathetic paralell between Creation's Humans and the Humans of this universe allow them to be more ready supply of essence. Earth was left alone as a preserve to keep stocks up but as humanity kept screwing themselves the league of alien species decided for more drastic measures, seeking to create humans that could enter Creation and thus create new life lines to feed their essence hunger - the Industrial Exalted. Would have minor reality warping powers (like changing gravity or how blood works) with some body moding stuff and their inbuilt story is all of them are Isekei'd from a Cyberpunk future to Creation and have to figure out how to get back, and if that is even worth it. Thematics would be cyberpunk, biotech and a little cosmic horror. Castes would be based on different sciences (given by their patron's to give them a fighting chance) and aspects on their particular patron race (they probably would be mostly unwilling exalts but some willing might be possible). Their patron races would not have supernaturally powerful individuals but have access to science and infrastructure that is beyond (non-exalted) human comprehension allowing them to do primordial like feats. Might also be using the minds of potential human geniuses to pay for the Law of Diminishment to avoid paying the price themselves.<br /> <br /> * Plague/Viral - Similar to above but make them the minions of a more powerful exalted type, might be demoted from being full exalted but instead being some sort of pseudo-exalted servitors. That or make them one caste of some sort of 'Chosen of Catastrophes'.<br /> <br /> * Supernal + Possible Emergents - I need a better name, but I would focus on the idea that each Primordial charm is basically an insane power boost in itself and unlike 2nd edition Infernals, I don't think learning a whole tree should be possible. Main inspirations would be people like Rincewind from Discworld (especially from Colour of Magic and Light Fantastic) or Bob Reynolds / Sentry / Void from MCU; a normal enough person given one supreme power that can reshape the world in seconds. Might replace them actually using the Primordial charm with the idea of their souls being transformed and they becoming like the Emergent exalted and using the summoning of their Peri as their main power. Another possibility is the charm is not a true exaltation but can grant it's power to a mortal (or even an exalt) but can change host at will, creation a sort of pseudo-exalt; heck the idea of person have a singular power and traveling around to find a new host (like All Might from My Hero Academia) could be an interesting concept but maybe not for a whole Exalted type.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> Thanks for the advice, I admit too many of my ideas start off with themes first before answering what role they could play in the universe.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Don't be ridiculous, Exalted of Volcanos would have castes based on how likely the are to erupt and change as they unleash their powers /joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T17:14:49-07:00","id":1553116,"title":"","content":"And I just realised as I post this two things;<br /> <br /> * My new Temporals are closer to the mad scientist trope than I could ever do with the Industrials.<br /> <br /> * Having a Supernal be part of a Exalted type with a lifecycle could be interesting (start of with a Primordial Charm in your head until you can find a new host and then the process of transferring it causes your soul structure to become two individual Peri (or maybe rename the souls as Espers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T23:35:46-07:00","id":1553163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553115#post1553115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Baaldam</a>, thanks for all that, I completely missed the name idea of Atavic/Atavistic exalted, and I thank you for all the ideas you put up for it. I was meaning to get back to this sooner but I kept being delayed so please don't hold it against me. If I do work on it do you mind if I take your ideas going forward?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of the forum, imho at least, is this &quot;chinese whispers of ideas game&quot;, where one person's starting concept evolves &amp; mutates with every other person that brings a bit of reinterpretation of its own, so totally go for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553115#post1553115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially the concept of Moonshadow being their patron, I like that - gives the concept of a previously unknown incarnae without having to make up a load of stuff or justifying why they're only now appearing. Although if I remember correctly Luna was made by taking several potential Lunar gods and pitching them into fighting each other until only one crawled out, so maybe one or more of them survived and became the new patron(s) after escaping from Lunar for so long.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole &quot;battle of the Lunas&quot; narrative from the Ink Monkeys is convoluted, confusing and contradicting like hell - and that's kind of very much by design, i guess. Maybe it happened and Luna has memories (and trauma) of it from consuming all the others, maybe it's all an incredibly barroque and abstruse exercise at simulation that existed only as whisps of memory in the multitudimous minds of certain Primordials living or dead and Luna knows them not except as weird segues from beings older than her.<br /> <br /> Maybe one proto-Luna grew out of the simulation between the coils of Oramus inside-out wings. Or the moments between recognition of death and drawing its last breath, a dying Primordial's thoughts turned to what would have the Divine Revolution been like if a different moon deity had been made and that reverie shaped itself into being as the Underworld came to be. Or Luna dreamed dreams of loss, guilt &amp; curiosity over siblings she never met in spirit flesh and in places between fugue and pure chaos these gained a life of its own. Or all are true, as 3 or more numimous beings each of a different origin gathered together around a common cause and secret the Maiden in Green has deigned not to unlock and share with Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553115#post1553115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not 100% sold on mixing them with the Plague Exalted but I think that could be repurposed as lesser servants of the Atavic exalted, a sort of forerunner they release to break populations and push people into being worthy of the Atavic exaltation while weakening enemy resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to clear things up, i was not quite speaking of merging the Plague Exalted with anyone else, so much as speaking of points of similarity, themes crossing and how one's idea of a patron can considerably affect power scale, theme and so on. I prefer to think of the &quot;Plaguexalted&quot; as more Liminal to the Atavistics' Abyssal or &quot;Sidereal to their Getimian&quot; so to speak, depending on where one wants to go with power levels, role in Creation and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553115#post1553115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Supernal + Possible Emergents - I need a better name, but I would focus on the idea that each Primordial charm is basically an insane power boost in itself and unlike 2nd edition Infernals, I don't think learning a whole tree should be possible. Main inspirations would be people like Rincewind from Discworld (especially from Colour of Magic and Light Fantastic) or Bob Reynolds / Sentry / Void from MCU; a normal enough person given one supreme power that can reshape the world in seconds. Might replace them actually using the Primordial charm with the idea of their souls being transformed and they becoming like the Emergent exalted and using the summoning of their Peri as their main power. Another possibility is the charm is not a true exaltation but can grant it's power to a mortal (or even an exalt) but can change host at will, creation a sort of pseudo-exalt; heck the idea of person have a singular power and traveling around to find a new host (like All Might from My Hero Academia) could be an interesting concept but maybe not for a whole Exalted type.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, the more you say on them, the more it feels like, imho at least, like the best place for these figures would be not as Exalts per se but sorcerers, with a Initiation path with shaping rituals and merits of its own centered on a theme of transcedence, beyond mortal, beyond spirit or perhaps even Primordial, something geared towards enhancing/improving oneself in all sorts of bizarre ways, possibly with tricks to boost sorcerous workings or using one's workings as a source of sorcerous motes, i don't know.<br /> <br /> But &quot;power cosmic from on high sparks to a flame in one's mind/heart/soul&quot; and &quot;you are crazy powerful from the get-go, the tricks you develop are just fine-tuning and extra tools in one's bag&quot; are things that speak far more of Sorcery than the charm trees of the Exalted to me. Just a thought.<br /> <br /> (Not ignoring the other stuff, just trying to focus on a few so we don't lose ourselves too much)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-14-2025, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-18T13:06:19-07:00","id":1553258,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Mr.Jaxus</a>, about the Industrials i have to say they are confused/lost aplenty on their own and trying to insert or merge them with the Prehuman/Shedim/Denisovan/Xenos definitely doesn't help.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of narrative bits around them, but they seem to struggle to form a coherent image and this lack of direction ends up turning into an additional stumbling block instead of helping to spark things or give focus.<br /> <br /> Instead of adding more to their narrative space - what instead runs the risk of making the whole package more overwhelming, imho - i would suggest you break it all down in parts, to them see how to piece them together, but bit by bit. So, let me start by summarizing the basic concept, with some commentary/doubts mixed in.<br /> <br /> - Autochthon, at some undefined point in time, connects to \u2018Earth\u2019, for reasons.<br /> - This apparently, due to some issue with the alien world that is this &quot;Earth&quot;, the Machine God struggling with its flagging health or both even, leads to nothing.<br /> - Until, centuries or millenia later, the Seal of Eight Divinities was cracked open and - new exaltations spring into existence, somehow. (Because Science??)<br /> - The exaltations start picking people to empower - on Creation, Autochtonia, Earth, all of the three? No idea, unclear, shake the magic 8-ball again.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Not trying to be snarky and also did not go into your original thread on Industrials, plenty to untangle on this version as is)<br /> <br /> So, from all of this i've come with two core issues:<br /> - Who is their patron/guide/etc, Autochthon, &quot;Earth scientific principles&quot; or what? This in particular seems to be a most tangled subject on the whole, like you are undecided either way, going back-&amp;-forth on a answer.<br /> <br /> - What do Industrials actually do or are supposed to? What would be their powerset? Do they use lots of charm/implants like Alchemicals, induce mutations on themselves and/or others with magical biotech, create a crazy amount of technomagical wonders or unlock those from others, all of the above?<br /> <br /> The last one i dare say is particularly important i dare say. The entities that make an exalt don't have to be an active or major part of their narrative, quite the contrary in most cases should be said. Damn, the <b><i>point </i></b>of some of the apocryphal chosen like Hearteaters and Umbrals is their creators are no more and they are completely on their own to decide their fates and what is right or not. So you can have an exalt that no one knows the origin of (not even themselves). Getimians were pretty much that early on.<br /> <br /> But you can't have an exalt without an idea of <b>what</b> they can do and how they do it. And to be fair i don't have much of an idea. The fact you mentioned both Aspects AND castes - even though those two things <i>cover basically the same niche</i> - seems to me like a sign that you have no idea either. You purloined some lore bits from Autochtonia and the Alchemicals, but not really sure of where to go with them.<br /> <br /> Solars get what normal people do (or dream of doing) and take it on larger-than-life/larger-than-the-world levels. Lunars shapechange and steal other beings forms. Sidereals see bits and pieces of the tapestry of Fate and then steer things in mind-boggling ways through their awareness. Abyssals go pedal to the metal on goth power. Alchemicals are more-than-human automatons with souls.<br /> <br /> <br /> What Industrials <b>are</b>? What do they <b>do </b>- and <b>how</b>? Find these things and you can get everything else in place later.<br /> <br /> <br /> And let me throw some ideas &amp; suggestions too, just to close things in a somewhat more constructive note.<br /> <br /> Having them be terrestrial tier could be beneficial, imho. Less raw power technically, but means they don't have numbers fixed in the low hundreds - what is pretty good narratively when it comes to fill out a whole world of craziness &amp; wonder and gives you the possibility of messing with bizarre mechanics around their reproduction - contamination? <b><i>Pollution</i></b> - with less worry of breaking anything.<br /> <br /> Plus, a less directly puisant charmset would be something of an incentive to explore evocations - what seems quite in synch to their name and thematic correlations, imho.<br /> <br /> Anyway, terrestrial tier might go well with aspects based on Autochtonian elements, bringing notes from the Realm of Brass &amp; Shadow and its chosen, while still being very much its own thing. The subject of contamination-pollution can also make for a twist of sorts on progenitive essence &amp; DB reproduction, with possible mix-up on the subject of aura, Limit-like stat or something akin to alchemical evolution into colossi or patropoli, Industrials having to struggle with their pollution potential to balance between growing power and eventual transformation into a literal hazard zone of a demesne or something similar.<br /> <br /> (Umbra means &quot;shadow&quot; - what if 'Earth', or a WoD-like reality, exist across the other side of Autochthon's dreamscape and the power behind its pollution, the Wyrm/Lindwurm/Conqueror Worm is a twisted 3rd circle Deva personifying Autochthon's malaise, an elemental dragon twisted by the Machine God's sickness or something in between?)<br /> <br /> Ramblings done for now. Hope you have fun with some of them at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-18-2025, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T07:08:29-07:00","id":1553265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553115#post1553115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * Temporals + Abstruse/Xana/Xeno + possibly Dichotimals + possibly Emergents + possibly Angelics + possibly Xeno; the idea was the Titan of Time's actually central concept was the line between Primordial and non-primordial; unfortunately some of his/her/their/it's ideas were horrid to the Primordials (like they should also die like lesser beings and be reincarnated), so they helped his/her/their/it's twin fetch's over throw him/her/them/it and alternate as Primordial and Fetch in an internal cycle that moves time forward; the five remaining souls (that didn't switch around between 3rd and 2nd level with each swapping of the primordial and fetch) became the Norns and sought some ways to test Primordials and Non-primordials, eventually sinking into a moment in the past to hide as they helped pushed the Primordial War and the rise of the Solars to see if they could test the line between Primordial and Non-primordial. Eventually the Norns made their own chosen to push the boundries and see if they can make things that challenge the lines set in sand by the Primordials (like the ban on time travel or raising the dead), with all Temporals being transgressors seeking to push various boundries. Castes would likely be based on what they're meant to challenge (like the other Exalted, the cycle of Reincarnation, Morality, Soul Structures, etc) with their time powers mostly used to protect them as they experiment. Emergent inspiration would be them developing soul structures like 2nd Edition Infernals; possibly Angelics and Xenos by having some of their castes focus on what it means to be of a particular species and what it means to embody a particular ideal to it's extremes. Dichotimal influnces would be present in how Norn's Primordial is in an internal conflict and a lot of their charms could have duality themes and focus on some nemesis or goal they have to challenge. But what ever I include I think I should focus on the Temporals + Abstruse/Xana/Xeno core and work from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the way it currently stands you seem to have all too many ingredients to juggle in the same dish. Seems like a recipe for trouble even before we get into the matter of developing a charmset - and the oliphant in the room, the narrative and mechanic nightmare rigmarole that time travel can be on its own. Because if you decide to delve into the subject, you'll have to cobble some framework and internal logic for it, paradoxes &amp; etc.<br /> <br /> Being the deity/titan/etc of time can be bonkers enough on itself - so i'd say, come up with how time manipulation/travel would work within the context of the Exalted setting, then use that to guide you in fleshing out the nature of the patron/guide or whatever idiosyncrasies it might possess.<br /> <br /> And then, as if to counter all that i just said, i remember something obscure from 2e that could perhaps offer inspiration to mixing Temporals and the Emergent/(Peri-users), i guess. Completely out of the blue, because why the hell not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scroll of the Monk, pg. 132</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The martial artist pulls gently at the mirror she holds before her enemy, and the reflection of her foe suddenly stands beside him. A close observer, however, sees something different about the double\u2014an edge to its smile, the slightest change in its movements. It\u2019s not the same person, they think \u2014 or, as the duplicates turn toward each other, is it?<br /> <br /> The martial artist may use Draw Forth One Shard on herself \u2014 but will rarely like what she calls. Masters have faced <b>versions of themselves as they might have been, as they wanted to be or as they feared they might become</b> \u2014 and few enjoyed the experience.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My original intent was just to cite <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_of_Persia#The_Sands_of_Time_series\" target=\"_blank\">Prince of Persia: The Sands of Time </a>games as possible reference for exploring/dealing with time travel rigmaroles in fantasy settings - but to be fair, those two things don't have to be mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> And speaking of dual natures.... what comes to be when a deity has a child with a demon, elemental or ghost? What nature will the spirit possess, how does its mixed heritage define or make it unlike its parents? What comes out then when a water-goddess and an elemental-demon flow into each other's waters so completely as to pool themselves into another being, reflecting both and yet neither in identity? Just a bout of stream-of-consciousness things going into each other, so to speak.\u200b<br /> <br /> Anyway, genderfluid elemental water demon-deity that can divide into a multitude of streams and yet also flow back into its whole undivided self, water bodies that can act as mirrors, showing what could have been, what might come to be and more, reflection that can be visual and/or a manifestation of introspection. Time in a water clock (instead of sand) of the adamant sky for glass. How does that work out for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-02-2025, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T02:56:13-07:00","id":1553795,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a>; sorry for not replying sooner, work has been hectic and draining; but thanks for everything. <br /> <br /> Some comments (not everything but for all your effort I want to say something):<br /> <br /> For Industrial Exalted: I hadn't originally intended 'industrial' to be the core theme, more 'scientific', and my idea was when I was first in college and didn't fully realise Creations physics were more spirit &amp; fate based than science based and tried to keep building on the original concept after I realised my mistake. However the idea of them being some sort of 'pollution' does sound fun and I could use if I ever focus on them.<br /> <br /> For Temporal Exalted; My current ideas for time travel was at low levels they can sort of go into a 'phantom' past like in a Christmas Carol, you can see but not interact. As they grow stronger than get more control of the past but as part of their nature history will try to minimise any change. For example if you go back in time to stop a historic tyrant, with enough time history would be rewritten so much of the damage and consequences still occured but had other causes. Wise Temporals use their time powers either to change very recent things (like being spotted by a guard), to discover information or to sow the seeds of plans after the fact (like going back in time to help a butler so they'll help you escape from their master's house). My ovely kitchen sink approach in my last post was based on the idea that their general theme could be challengers to the natural order; just as their time travel breaks all the rules, each caste would be created to test and break a rule of Creation.<br /> <br /> For Atavistic Exalted; I'd probably drop the link to Plague Exalted - I thought it would be fun to have several Exalted tied together in a lifecycle thing but my concepts for Atavistic share nothing in common with Plague other than creating messed up communities of humans; I keep imagining Atavistic making communities of human cultists morphing into what ever pre-human race they draw power from ala deep one hybrids from the Cthulhu mythos while Plague exalted are a literal plague and the survivors mostly turn to this new community of empowered survivors they find themselves in. By binding the two I was imagining a life cycle of a the Plague Exalted being unleashed on an area and while most survivors merely become more Plague Exalted, certain ones would tap into a deeper power and become Atavistic Exalted; however in retreospect that doesn't make much sense. My current idea is that each time an Atavistic dies, their exaltation creates a pocket dimension (which I would call a Labyrinth if that wasn't used for a major part of the underworld) which sucks mortals in and imprissons them until one manages to be beat the maze and puzzles of the pocket dimension and wins the exaltation; the rest die as sacrifices to empower the Exaltation as no (or at least minimal) initial price was paid for them - the Atavistic might now have the pocket dimension to reshape as a lair to hide in and use as a base for themselves and any mutated followers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T14:25:42-07:00","id":1553841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553795#post1553795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Baaldam</a>; sorry for not replying sooner, work has been hectic and draining; but thanks for everything.<br /> <br /> Some comments (not everything but for all your effort I want to say something):</div> </div> </div> </div>Life has a way with creating hurdles to get on the way of our enjoyment &amp; play, it happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553795#post1553795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Industrial Exalted: I hadn't originally intended 'industrial' to be the core theme, more 'scientific', and my idea was when I was first in college and didn't fully realise Creations physics were more spirit &amp; fate based than science based and tried to keep building on the original concept after I realised my mistake. However the idea of them being some sort of 'pollution' does sound fun and I could use if I ever focus on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much a matter of Creations physics being more spirit based per se, since while deities might have influence over their purviews, they are not dependent on these beings for their existence. Gods and goddesses are stewards, but not the concepts manifest per se. Though yeah, it follows a idiosyncratic set of rules its own, where Craft, Lore &amp; Occult mix &amp; match, sort of covering in a blurry manner that mental space where the sciences fill in on the world as we understand it.<br /> <br /> All of that said, <b>exalted </b>are a whole different matter. <b><i>Someone</i></b> must choose people to empower with the miracle of exaltation, even if in an indirect &quot;codified the criteria of approval&quot; manner. Thermodynamics or Quantum mechanics do not empower people or somesuch, so there must be some sort of cosmology working alongside the laws of nature of this other world and entities somehow connected to it, even if from an outsider perspective - like Ketu in the deep Wyld supposedly using the Dream-Souled to learn more of and/or interact by proxy with Creation, for example. So fleshing out some elements of this &quot;Earth&quot; and how like - and unlike - ours can go a long way in giving things a clearer form to work with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553795#post1553795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Temporal Exalted; My current ideas for time travel was at low levels they can sort of go into a 'phantom' past like in a Christmas Carol, you can see but not interact. As they grow stronger than get more control of the past but as part of their nature history will try to minimise any change. For example if you go back in time to stop a historic tyrant, with enough time history would be rewritten so much of the damage and consequences still occured but had other causes. Wise Temporals use their time powers either to change very recent things (like being spotted by a guard), to discover information or to sow the seeds of plans after the fact (like going back in time to help a butler so they'll help you escape from their master's house). My ovely kitchen sink approach in my last post was based on the idea that their general theme could be challengers to the natural order; just as their time travel breaks all the rules, each caste would be created to test and break a rule of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of the Shadows of the Ancient Past spell, that might be good fodder for reference. You might also look into Investigation and Lore charms too, for that &quot;unearthing the lost details&quot; or &quot;bringing a new perspective on facts&quot; angles. Solar Occult charms &quot;Soul Projection Method&quot; and &quot;Immortal Soul Vigil&quot; are also worth mentioning for the kind of bizarre mental gymnastics of memory, past, present &amp; potentially rewriting parts of either one may find between them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553795#post1553795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Atavistic Exalted; I'd probably drop the link to Plague Exalted - I thought it would be fun to have several Exalted tied together in a lifecycle thing but my concepts for Atavistic share nothing in common with Plague other than creating messed up communities of humans; I keep imagining Atavistic making communities of human cultists morphing into what ever pre-human race they draw power from ala deep one hybrids from the Cthulhu mythos</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometime ago i toyed a bit with something pretty much along those lines with the Lintha, using the Kimbery themes of fluidity, corrosion, accretion and so on to reinterpreted them as a race ever-changing through cycles of consumption and dillution where they incrementally adapt and mold themselves to the beings they confront and interact with, among other bits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553795#post1553795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">while Plague exalted are a literal plague and the survivors mostly turn to this new community of empowered survivors they find themselves in. By binding the two I was imagining a life cycle of a the Plague Exalted being unleashed on an area and while most survivors merely become more Plague Exalted, certain ones would tap into a deeper power and become Atavistic Exalted; however in retreospect that doesn't make much sense..</div> </div> </div> </div>It would require considerable work and kitbashing to even form an image of where to go to make sense of such a cycle of two exalt types not only working but <i>springing forth</i> together. Yeah, probably better to drop that for the sake of your sanity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, chosen of the disease gods could be a thing their own, a subset of Exigents (much like the Sovereigns of the colectivity of city gods) with a whole set of bizarre agendas their own but that somehow lead them to occasional strife with the Atavistic, maybe because some of the things and places that resonate with Atavistic essence and the dead species they represent share some common themes (rot, carcasses, still waters, strange fumes, etc) with disease vectors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1553795#post1553795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current idea is that each time an Atavistic dies, their exaltation creates a pocket dimension (which I would call a Labyrinth if that wasn't used for a major part of the underworld) which sucks mortals in and imprissons them until one manages to be beat the maze and puzzles of the pocket dimension and wins the exaltation; the rest die as sacrifices to empower the Exaltation as no (or at least minimal) initial price was paid for them - the Atavistic might now have the pocket dimension to reshape as a lair to hide in and use as a base for themselves and any mutated followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some sort of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hedge\" target=\"_blank\">hedge </a>you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-20-2025, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T14:55:31-07:00","id":1554130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1552406#post1552406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Personally, to mess around further with the &quot;dead things not quite as gone as expected trying to make a comeback&quot; angle, i'm tempted to suggest Moonshadow, the goddess of <b><i>lunar </i></b>eclipses no one talks about though it should - possibly an aspect of Luna that was lost/gained &quot;life&quot; of her own sometime between the first solar eclipse and the formation of the Underworld with the first Primordial death. Also messing around with the whole &quot;between lunars &amp; abyssals&quot; narrative space a bit]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I do more reading up on this Lunar Eclipse goddess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T15:11:53-07:00","id":1554208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1554130#post1554130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where can I do more reading up on this Lunar Eclipse goddess?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess probably nowhere, since she's 100% &quot;entity i came up with on-the-spot, from playing with lore bits &amp; themes&quot; and &quot;<i>the goddess no one talks about though it should</i>&quot; was kind of funny wordplay on that from my part, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> She's wholy a product of improptu homebrew and improvised personal fanon that was inspired by our discussion of themes, powerset and so on, the whole &quot;lunar-ish with some hint of abyssal but not quite either&quot; narrative space, so i stole the name of the deathknights NotEclipse caste, riffed the concept from Glories to the Most High of the aspects of Luna being stillborn proto-lunar deities consumed by the one we know in some surreal multi-dimensional dream battle conceived by some Primordials in an undefined time long, long ago and the curious absence of any mention of a lunar eclipse caste among Luna's chosen to shape up a near-Incarna entity out of it.<br /> <br /> But well, she's an all-around homebrew deity, so there's no canon lore that you infringe by making her according to whatever you feel like taking inspiration from.<br /> We can develop her if you are up to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-01-2026, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-30T16:22:12-07:00","id":1560276,"title":"","content":"So I have been thinking on these ideas but not working on them but I do have directions for them the Atavistic and Temporal Exalted.<br /> <br /> Temporals: Still base idea of a chosen of the Primordial of Time (who alternates between Chronos and Aion for Primordial and Fetch soul); they make one big jump into the past when they Exalt; going back into the past to fix a regret in exchange for some missions either Chronos or Aion. Most of their powers deal with the flow of time, their mission and change; might have some way to make more regular time travel trips but have some limit based on the continuum of history (kill x, but someone else rises up to take over their role in history) or needing to do jobs for Chronos or Aion to gain jumps - overall a espionage theme and theme of not knowing who your allies and enemies really are. I had some ideas they could be specifically survivors of some world ending threat that had a goal of trying to stop that crisis by any means possible, but I dump it due kinda means the world can't really be threatened as a Temporal would be sent back to stop it.<br /> <br /> Atavistics: Either chosen by Lunar's shadow/blood who was the omen of doom for a people (saving some of the dying species and later using them to create the Atavistic Exalted), a collection of the souls of races slain in the Primordial War who people's ghost mass sacrificed themselves to create Exaltations to get back at the other Exalted, or a Primordial who sacrificed their non-fetch souls to create Exaltations and enter a near-death coma rather than be part of the Neverborn or Yozis. Which ever way, they are bound to various pocket universes called a 'Sidhe', which reflect on the environments of their fallen species. When an Atavistics dies, their Sidhe slow warps into a dungeon called a 'guantlet', any mortal that enters through the portals is both drawn and challenged to the core; the first one to do so will gain the Exaltation. Mortals and creatures in Sidhes will mutate into 'spawn', recreations of their Atavistic's species, which while they don't have direct control over the Atavistic exalted can influence and draw power from. Will have access to Necromancy over Sorcery. I did think of a concept of their being the replacement soul structure for a Primordial with three ranks of Exalted which determine the power of their charms, essence powers, sidhe and level of Necromancy (so a 3rd circle picks 2nd circles who picks 1st circle), but I'm not fully sold on it. Overall feel is a combination a genestealer cults from Warhammer 40k, the movie Evolution, Dungeon Capturers from Magi-The Labyrinth Of Magic and Beast the Primordial from Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-01T03:31:18-07:00","id":1560303,"title":"","content":"Okay, I did have some thoughts on Industrials but they're all over the place so to summarise:<ul><li>I need to rename them, my ultimate goal is a science based one but the name &quot;Industrial&quot; keeps being a creative thorn. &quot;Scientific&quot; Exalted doesn't have the same ring to it. Core concept is they based on mad scientists and even if not intellectually inclined before, their Exaltation pushes them to understand and test reality.</li> <li>Not fully sure if they'd still have Autochthon as their patron, a distant source of power in their creation or not involved at all. Possible other patrons include a Primordial of lack/entropy</li> <li>Main idea is Autochton found a side dimension to the Wyld (basically our universe) and unable to explore it fully gave the local humans a drone/token called the Earthstar which was encoded with a way for them to contact Autochthon when they were advanced enough along with some of his design notes. As their world was dying the finally found out what it was capable of but some bright spark realised it could do more; a lot more. They reverse engineered the processes to create a near infinite energy system; all it required was a massive loss of 'para-mental potential' focused on a 'high para-mental potential' individual who would be cast into Creation/Autochthonia; creating a rift that pours in essence into their world that they capture and use to produce electricity. To mass produce this method they've taken to seeding worlds with human populations, creating artificial histories and when a century or two pass they choose a candidate and then mass harvest the rest of the planet to send people into Creation/Auchthonia as new Exalts.</li> <li>Either that or Industrials are created by their patrons as testers for Creation's laws of (meta)physics, designed to push the boundaries in ways they were not meant to be.</li> <li>Might have a 3/4 level structure based off academic achievement: Zeroth circle (undergrad; person with potential but no access to powers yet), First circle (bachelors ~ terrestrial exalted), Second circle (masters ~ celestial exalted) and finally third circle (doctorate ~ solaroid). This progression would be based on their development of a special power called a 'Magnum Opus', a major redefinition/aberation of the laws of reality they advance over time.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T11:40:18-07:00","id":1560351,"title":"","content":"You might want to dig through Promethean to see if it has some names to use, since it seems like the closest you'll get to a treatment of modern-day investigative inquiry. You could even pry loose the concept of the Alchemical Demiurge from 2e and call them Demiurgic Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-06T15:06:42-07:00","id":1560414,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the recommendation for name sources; but can I ask what the &quot;Alchemical Demiurge&quot; is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T07:25:49-07:00","id":1560617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1560414#post1560414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the recommendation for name sources; but can I ask what the &quot;Alchemical Demiurge&quot; is?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mortal artificer-savants that serve as intermediaries empowered by Autochthon in the making of Alchemical Exalted.<br /> <br /> Also, long time no see. Almost an year since we last messed with this all, no? Give some time to get the mental gears back to spinning in the right manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-14-2026, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T07:56:23-07:00","id":1560635,"title":"","content":"My impressions so far:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1560276#post1560276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temporals: Still base idea of a chosen of the Primordial of Time (who alternates between Chronos and Aion for Primordial and Fetch soul); they make one big jump into the past when they Exalt; going back into the past to fix a regret in exchange for some missions either Chronos or Aion. Most of their powers deal with the flow of time, their mission and change; might have some way to make more regular time travel trips but have some limit based on the continuum of history (kill x, but someone else rises up to take over their role in history) or needing to do jobs for Chronos or Aion to gain jumps - overall a espionage theme and theme of not knowing who your allies and enemies really are. I had some ideas they could be specifically survivors of some world ending threat that had a goal of trying to stop that crisis by any means possible, but I dump it due kinda means the world can't really be threatened as a Temporal would be sent back to stop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest putting the Patron, whatever one decides to name it and true identity/nature is or not, in the backburner....<br /> <br /> (And then midway through writing, something DOES pop-up - the Eternal Sandglass, keeper of time and its cycles, master-mistress of the neverending story of grains of existence past, present &amp; future trickling into each other, blurring the lines of ends and beginings between countless sand &amp; all-encompassing crystal globes, interlocked. Cecelyne, SWLIHN, whose soul is it, if not both or neither. Buried &amp; erased in the dance of the sands and spheres...)<br /> <br /> ...to focus instead on your exalts, their flavor, personality, the kind of stories and themes one might explore through them.<br /> Look at those short summaries of the many exalt types (that also happen to include at least Liminals &amp; Exigents, if memory tricks me not) in the 3e corebook for examples to ground you on framing your own creations.<br /> <br /> But speaking of &quot;Temporals&quot; proper:<br /> - They interact with time, but how, in what way does it influence their charmset or give them some sort of unique toolset, like Heart's Blood for Lunars or Astrology for Sidereals?<br /> <br /> - Are future and past fixed or mutable and if the later, what effects may a time paradox or temporal loop have on the exalt or the world around it?<br /> <br /> - Isn't there potential for issues with causality and if so, might not that attract attention or opposition of Sidereals and/or Getimians (that kind of happen to be alternate timelines Chosen, if memory tricks me not)?<br /> <br /> Anyway, you need to focus on the Exalt side of things instead of cosmology stuff related to a patron they might not even hear of. I would advise using Exigents, with maybe some Essence mixed in, to make a single prototype to see where things go, as a sprinboard to find out what you want or not from them at least, on the mechanics/playstyle front.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1560276#post1560276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atavistics: Either chosen by Lunar's shadow/blood who was the omen of doom for a people (saving some of the dying species and later using them to create the Atavistic Exalted), a collection of the souls of races slain in the Primordial War who people's ghost mass sacrificed themselves to create Exaltations to get back at the other Exalted, or a Primordial who sacrificed their non-fetch souls to create Exaltations and enter a near-death coma rather than be part of the Neverborn or Yozis. Which ever way, they are bound to various pocket universes called a 'Sidhe', which reflect on the environments of their fallen species. When an Atavistics dies, their Sidhe slow warps into a dungeon called a 'guantlet', any mortal that enters through the portals is both drawn and challenged to the core; the first one to do so will gain the Exaltation. Mortals and creatures in Sidhes will mutate into 'spawn', recreations of their Atavistic's species, which while they don't have direct control over the Atavistic exalted can influence and draw power from. Will have access to Necromancy over Sorcery. I did think of a concept of their being the replacement soul structure for a Primordial with three ranks of Exalted which determine the power of their charms, essence powers, sidhe and level of Necromancy (so a 3rd circle picks 2nd circles who picks 1st circle), but I'm not fully sold on it. Overall feel is a combination a genestealer cults from Warhammer 40k, the movie Evolution, Dungeon Capturers from Magi-The Labyrinth Of Magic and Beast the Primordial from Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more i think about it, the more your ideas about Atavistic's exaltation process, the more something like the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hedge\" target=\"_blank\">Hedge</a> of Changeling the Lost, a Labyrinth-Jungle of sorts, inhabited by strange ephemeral fauna that mixes the memories of extinct species with the dream-musings of its masters, the animal fathers of beast long gone alongside the dream/shades/embers of hierarchs &amp; hive-queens of lost races of elemental beings straddling the lines between beast, deity or people in the role of Neverborn/Deathlord-like patrons.<br /> <br /> <br /> And on an aside about Scientific/Industrials/Artificers/Experimentalists or whatever other name you prefer, the summary's ideas seem to be as much (or more) about &quot;Earth in Exalted setting somehow&quot; than about a new/unknown Exalt type.<br /> <br /> So they are mad scientists or builders of strange wonders? How does that play out, how do they mess with the Craft, Occult, Investigation or Lore rules to build or discover new crazy things? What use are the other skills for in their case?<br /> <br /> Sidereals might make a good example of how to take a more &quot;niche&quot; concept/role, in the form of the seer/vizier/guide and through its lens fleshing out charmsets for all skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-21-2026, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T17:39:05-07:00","id":1561441,"title":"","content":"Okay, sorry for the late reply; this has been a busy time with personal matters and running a game but I am currently typing out all for all three but I've only completed Temporals so I'll post that for now:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MsoTableGrid\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Name</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporal</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Rough Summary</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Chosen of time, their powers focus on is manipulating the flow. They are tied to Quests given by their patrons; their lives are shaped by suspicion, trickery and subterfuge not unlike most spy stories as they try to find out who is friend and foe.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">TLDR: timetravelers who play as knights righting wrongs but actually stuck in a chronological spy thriller.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Power Levels and Count</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Celestial; unknown exact count, but rarely more than 30-50 at any one time except at Gatherings, which can see hundreds being chosen at the same time.<br /> <br /> Some theorise that their count is even smaller as Chronos and Aion just recycle Exaltations through time as linear time might not be a series concern for them; if this is the case there might only be a handful of Exaltations reused through the past, present and future with Exalts interacting with others with the same shard in a most paradoxical manner.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Can live to around a millenium, but each attribute has a charm that grants a form of immortality as it\u2019s pinnacle achievement, however all of these come with a price that must be paid or complications which limit their effectiveness (like having to drain the youth out of others). Only one such charm can be bought per Temporal.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Themes</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Time, Speed, Moments, Countering Specific Targets, Missions, Second Chances, Hope, Confusion, Angelic Inspirations, Sand, the flow of time, change in people, Spy craft, missions, duty; maybe music.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Patron</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Titan of Time, the Primordial who reigns over time. Unfortunately to produce the glorious flow of time, the Primordial must flip between with their fetch soul; this eternal dance between Chronos and Aion defines the Primordial and shape their goals both long term and short term. Both sides have vast knowledge of the past and future, even to degrees beyond the Maidens, but are also held back by their constant infighting and conflicting goals. They entered the Primordial War on both sides, with Temporal Exalted fight to defend and kill daeva, often in ways and for reasons that seemed contradictory:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Aion is the more distant personality, favouring the rules and laws of the Primordials with a strict top down approach. However they are also more invested in the continued existence of others and are time as a constant a repetitive force on life. Their current goals seem to be finding a way for the Neverborn to reincarnate to the restore either Authothchon or Gaia to the supreme power in Yu Shan.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Chronos is the more involved personality, favouring the rise and fall of challenge, so much as to support the Incarnae in rebellion even before the Primordial War. Chronos is the flow and change innate to time and believes the Exalted over throwing the Yozis to not only be a good thing, but the fundamental nature of reality and seems to be look for some new revolution. Their current goals seem to be trying to overthrow the Realm while also preparing for the next Dragon Blooded uprising against the rule of Celestial Exalted and creating a new species to challenge humanity.</span></li> </ul> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Titan of Time\u2019s other third circle souls are divided into three groups; The Aioni (aligned with Aion), the Chronosi (aligned to Chronos) and the Titani (unaligned with either and more focused on the general good of the Primordials needs rather than one side or the other\u2019s power plays). Most of the time the various Daeva are hidden in personal sanctums across Creation, although one, Hurn Du\u2019ul, pretends to be the God of Sand in Yu Shan, using this position to keep an eye on Temporals and give them a helping hand.<br /> <br /> Chronos and Aion dwell in Nusquama, the capital city of Outopia, a continent sized island that is one second ahead of Creation that also has vast palatial estates for the other Daeva while replicas of Creation\u2019s greatest people (past, present and future) prance and enjoy themselves while masking the bitter shadow war that is fought every moment in that false paradise.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Exaltation Method</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I had two thoughts on this:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Each Temporal is invited to take an exaltation in order to jump back in time and resolve a singular issue or regret in their life; they can either have their mind sent back to their old body or have a full body. Either way in exchange for this second chance they have to take on a Quest from their patron (Chronos or Aion) which acts a Defining Principle. I prefer this one as it\u2019s more personal to the Exalt and is less world (re)defining.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Each Temporal is literal Exalted as the world is ending and sent back in time (ala Kyle Reese from the Terminator or James Cole from 12 Monkeys) to stop it. While I think it\u2019s cool and adds instant stakes, it also has two major negative points; the first is that it robs world destroying threats of their potential (as someone can always go back in time to stop it) and it give all temporal exalts too much of a narrative weight and can redefine campaigns. </span></li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Backstory+ History</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Titan of Time was always a fickle being at the best of times; unable to choose between their two selves, Chronos and Aion, about who was fetch and who was the primordial. This conflict was temporarily resolved by Autochthon by creating a system where they each take turns being the Primordial and fetch; from this was born time, and the rest is history.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Unfortunately this left the Titan of Time with little real presence in Creation, as one version would flicker in and out of reality in tandem with the other, leaving only their main bodies stuck in Yu Shan. Eventually Aion and Chronos were side lined due to their conflicting goals and inability to form long term relationships with the other Primordials. Aion continued to seek their favour while Chronos tried to find rapport with their lesser beings spawned by the Primordials, from the lowest mortal to the highest Incarnae. However they both still found it hard to actual exist and actually shape the affairs of Creation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">And then the Exalted came.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporals were not created for either side of the Primordial War but instead as personal servants of Aion and Chronos; they had initially presented their petition to Autochthon in exchange for vague assurances of helping in the war, but the Titan of Time gave their chosen some little modifications \u2013 allowing them to receive direct Quests from the Primordial (or it\u2019s fetch) that would be reward in the course of time, creating a legion of mercenaries that allowed Chronos and Aion to finally shape affairs in Creation; and while Aion did favour the Primordials and lend them aid, Chronos\u2019 support of the Solars and the Incarnae allowed him to butter them up after the war and spare any real repercussions. However they did slowly build a sanctuary, an island one second ahead of all things to hide in for the same reason Autochthon fled Creation; the Exalts were a threat.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Temporals joined the early Deliberative, although some were barred for their service to the Primordials during the Divine Revolution. However the Temporals still had some loyalty to Aion, and their Quests were viewed with suspicion by the other Exalted, to say nothing of their rumoured secret of time travel and jealousy it breed (or annoyance amongst Sidereals). Eventually they were rooted from their positions of power or new (non-temporal) heirs found when one their number fell. Once over a hundred Temporals sat with their Celestial comrades, by the Evening of Peace only one bitter representative remained and no other Temporals were known to exist.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">And then the First Gathering occurred; at least 319 Temporals all exalted at the same time and started on various Quests, some seeking to kill and remove Solars and Lunars, others seeking to save them. The sudden chaos of war and rebellions was fuelled by the corruption of the Great Curse as mortals and Dragon Blooded saw a chance against actually and perceived tyrannies \u2013 and it was so sudden and intense the day before was dubbed the Evening of Peace. The First Gathering was quickly stopped, but the brutality needed to stop it was unimaginable intense and helped water the seeds of the Usurpation centuries later.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It was also the start of \u2018Gatherings\u2019, when large number of Temporal Exalted were chosen and sent into Creation, often with contradictory Quests, sowing chaos and confusion into the world. Gatherings can see hundreds of Exalts pop up, but most die with the first couple of weeks as the find themselves in misremembered surroundings or targeted by Wyld Hunts; when the Gatherings end, there is rarely more than 50 Temporals surviving and during most of the time there seems to be less than 30 Temporals in Creation (either as survivors from a Gathering or as new Exalts). Gatherings do not happen to any particular time table or regular reason; while the Great Contagion saw one (which broke all records at nearly a 1000 Temporals appeared to fight to defend Creation, and no known survivors are recorded (although some Temporals claim to have been around then and escape by jumping into the future, which is something they are known to be able (and willing) to do)) not all major events see Gathers (like the Usurpation).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Most of the time during the period between the First Gathering and the Great Contagion many (if not most) Temporals belonged to an underground movement called the Hourglass Conclave; it taught and guided young Temporals without requiring to go to one of the Souls of the Titan of Time and get caught up in their politics while hiding the Temporal Exalts from the watchful eye of the Deliberative. It also ironed out disputes between Temporals arising from conflicting (or near conflicting) Quests and other issues. The Hourglass helped the fledgling Silver Pact, via intel, shared resources and guidance for escaping Lunars. Both Aion and Chronos were disgruntled with the organisation and tried to destroy the Hourglass Conclave, but it\u2019s doom came from the ruin of the Great Contagion; too much of it\u2019s infrastructure was tied to mortal run safe houses and strong holds at the edge of Creation; the Contagion killed too many people for it to survive and many Temporals that Exalted afterwards were given Quests to dismantle the last of it, not to say of Sidereals using the chaos as an opportunity to make notable Dragon blood heroes by looting it\u2019s artefact stashes and killing senior members while the Silver Pact absorbed those who fled into their open arms.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Now-a- days most Temporals are lonely heroes appointed by distant patrons with no connection to their wider history. But the Time of Tumult is quickly becoming a major Gathering and new opportunities await; especially for those to whom both the past and future are open opportunities.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Relations with others</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporals biggest enemies are unfortunately the fellow Temporals; their Quests are set by the conflicting Chronos and Aion; and even within the Cells (group of Temporals) of those aligned to the same persona, they can have radically different Quests that contradict with each other. This is made many older Temporals suspicious of their own kind. The reasons for this seems to be due Temperals coming from different points of the future where Aion\u2019s and/or Chronos\u2019 goals have changed with changing times and realities; as new Temporals Quests revealing subtle things about the future to their patrons that further change their plans and shape new Quests given to Temporals over time. The Hourglass Conclave helped alleviate many of these issues in the past but was neither fully successful (as not all Temporals joined it) and is currently non-existent. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fair Folk also have a major bone to pick with the Temporals; their patron is one of the major members of the Primordials who set of the forging of Creation through the creation of time and the subsequent formation of causality wrecking their nice little stories. This has been made worse by ages of Temporals hiding out near freeholds and the edges of Creation leading to longing running conflicts between them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Sidereals, along with the rest of the Bureau of Destiny, are also a major enemy of the Temporals; Even their mere Exaltation causes enough issues with Fate and Destiny that removing them is seen as priority to say nothing of sheer amount of Paradox some of their charms produce (and speaking nothing if the legends of time travel are true). It is for this reason that Sidereals and Yu Shan have one of the highest kill counts of Temporals and maintain the largest via Wyld hunts back by them; Temporals are known Anethema to all Immaculates and the Realm\u2019s looted many of the Hourglass Conclave\u2019s cells to ensure that no Temporals could interfere with the Scarlet Empress\u2019 nascent empire (which considering the rumours of the Temporals martyring themselves to help her take the Imperial Manse might be more than a little hypocritical).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Outside of the Bureau of Destiny gods and elementals having varying opinions on Temporals but few as vitriolic as the Sidereals; some even joke the Visiers are only jealous of Temporals due to their broader (if less accurate and \u2018blurry\u2019) insights into the future not limited between what is in and out of fate. Some gods and elementals support the Temporals due to support the Hourglass Conclave gave in the past, others are tempted by Hurn Du\u2019ul\u2019s whispers or dreams of a better future pro-Primordial that doesn\u2019t involve turning to the Yozis or neverborn. All in all, Yu Shan is more negative to the Temporals, spirit courts in Creation are more open to them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Lunars is interested in Temporals, some see recreating the Hourglass conclave to repay old debts or giving them support as proxies against their enemies, but even the most ardent allies of them know the fickleness of Temporals and their patrons. As such the Silver Pact has taken a cautious approach to Temporals but is more than willing to help them if it helps Lunars as well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Getimians are usually willing to find some sort of kinship, as Rakan Thulio holds a level of respect for them and sees them as potential allies against Yu Shan. So far he has been rewarded with some allies and associates, but many Temporals are wary of him and the Getimians and Rakan Thulio is aware at least 2 Temporals have been sent to interfere with his goals.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Yozis range from optimistic to disgusted with Temporals; Aion is more aligned to them than the Incarnae, and Aioni Temporals have helped them in the past, but Chronos is against them. The former rulers of Creation know of the full extent of Temporal\u2019s time powers, and are aware of all timelines they create and destroy by their endeavours, so they are often invaluable sources of knowledge to Temporals, but they will only offer this at a steep price in favours. Infernal Exalted are warned of Temporals and their ways but are allowed to approach them however they wish.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The common undead are generally as wary of Temporals as other other Exalts, but don\u2019t treat them differently. Ancient ghosts and Death Lords tend to know more of their powers and seek to limit their Quests in the Underworld. The Neverborn especially want Aioni Temporals kept in line as it is known they seek to reincarnate the Neverborn in one of Aion\u2019s long term plans to remake the Primordials.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Autochthon himself is neutral to the Temporals, he insisted on the Quest system rather than being straight servants of the Titan of Time to ensure the Exalted had free will, but he saw them fight on both sides of the war and dislikes the Titan of Time in general (for being a jerk to him in the past) but tries take his chosen as individuals. The average Autochthonian has little to no knowledge of Temporals, and only the Divine ministers (and their servants) have accurate records on them \u2013 mostly as Temporals have no place in Autochthonia; however as the Seal of 8 Divinities is broken, Temporals are starting to appear in the Realm of Brass and Shadow.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporals best chance for allies are Solars, who similarly have a massive disconnect with their history and a lack of pre-build social supports making them kindred groups trying to survive in the Time of Tumult.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Castes and Anima</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temperals have animas in muted colours, especially beige, but pale blues, pinks and faded greens are also common; their animas glow but do not shine like solars. I envision them as being one of four options:</span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Regular animas \u2013 regular anima barriers like other exalts that are symbolic representations of their character and ideals.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Wings \u2013 originally for the idea of Temporals as being chosen to stop world ending events and have and angel theme for them; might give it miss because of that but still sounds interesting. Either way it would allow them to fly in addition to other effect and each set of wings is unique to it\u2019s exalt.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Music \u2013 instead of a traditional light based anima their soul manifests it\u2019s power as a musical compliment to the Temporal, which while it\u2019s tempo and tune is depended on what the Temporal is doing, the specific notes are distinct to each Temporal. Might require adding an overall musical theme to Temporals and not instantly as easy to grasp for players are detriments in my eyes.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Similar to Sidereals, they animas are not obvious, appearing only as a caste mark and several lines flowing across their body in arcane patterns, all of which can be covered with heavy clothing</span></li> </ol> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In the most likely case: 3 castes; Past, Present and Future:<br /> <br /> Past are those who focus on learning from the past and protecting it\u2019s legacy; Their caste mark is an inverted twilight mark. Note sure as to potential powers, but possibly when Burning the Temporal can regain one mote per success whenever they succeed on a roll they use their excellencies on (up to the amount they spent on the excellency). Strength, Charisma and Intelligence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Present are the fast thinks and trouble shooters who live in the here and now. Their caste mark is a ring with a line running vertically down the middle splitting it in two. Again not sure of their anima effects but one possibility is they can spend Initiative instead of essence to power excellencies; others would focus on speed and reactions. Dexterity, Wits and Appearance</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Future are plotters, planners and survivors. Their cast mark is either a small ring with seven lines spiralling out of it or a small ring with two outstretched lines going upwards. Potential effects are able to transfer extra successes on a roll they used an excellency up to a related follow up roll as a charm dice; also can seal vows like Solar Eclipse castes, although instead of cursing oath breakers they cast them several day/weeks/years/decades/centuries depending on their essence level. Stamina, Perception and Manipulation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Other possible caste solutions are reasons for the mortal having regrets and making the bargain (Love/Prosperity/Revenge/Etc) or over various timescales (moments, days, seasons/ lifetimes/centuries).</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Material Resonances</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Starmetal or Adamant. If they had their own material it would be some sort of some sort of glass made of sand from Temporal aligned manses or Outopia.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporal demesnes and manses are rare and tend to be in sandy places, in silent places or between clusters of other demesnes. Outopia is also dotted with many of them, which are often tied to points in Creation (and one or two in Yu Shan) that serve as anchors to hold that dimension in place.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Charm focuses</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporal Charms tend to allow them to achieve things faster and find solutions based on manipulation of the time flow; however they are not as tough as lunars, as glorious as solars or have the subtle strangeness of sidereal charms. Their charms are attribute based and have different themes beyond their initially application. Additionally, each attribute might be topped off with an Immortality charm that can be used to extend their lifespan, but often at some sort of cost; additionally each Temporal can only learn one such charm so their choice has to be good.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Strength: Support of the Past \u2013 focuses on reclaiming, repeating actions and utilising physical historic strength (or weakness). Charm ideas included attacking without wound penalties, creating a slip stream so allies can add your successes to their dice pool or throw ranged attacks back at their sender. Not sure what the Immortality charm is specifically, but might involve cutting off some of your flesh and putting it in a pot filled with preservatives; when you die of old age the flesh regrows into a new young body.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Intelligence: Secrets of the Past \u2013 Focuses on giving the user insights into the past and allowing them to know things that have been lost. Charm ideas included psychometry to read the history of an object, turning objects back to their base materials or tapping into past life memories. Not sure for what the Immortality charm is.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Charisma: Glory of the Past \u2013 Focuses on encourage others, nostalgia and tradition. Charm concepts include giving targets visions of the Primordial\u2019s minds to either drive them insane or influence them (depending on their nature), making others see you as being under one of their intimacies if you would have counted as such in the past, or breaking armies with vision of your past deeds. The Immortality charm makes the user spread stories about themselves, as long as they live up to the legend, their life is extended.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Dexterity: Act in the Moment \u2013 Focuses on doing as much as possible in the here and now, often giving the user bursts of speed beyond the capabilities of others. Charm concepts include stopping gravity for a few seconds to walk on air, making a flurry of attacks without penalties and move rapidly across the land. The Immortality charm involves constantly moving place to place to literally avoid death and aging.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Wits: Study the Moment \u2013 Focuses on being aware of the here and now, taking in details faster than other and extending the user\u2019s awareness. Charm concepts include swapping initiative values with a target at the start of combat, instantly picking up all details in a room and scrying nearby targets related to their quest.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Appearance: Focuses on fitting in the here and now, it\u2019s is central to the espionage aspects of Temporals, as it allows them to fit into situations via minor shapeshifting, adopting cultural ticks and the like. Charm concepts include changing their apparent age, stopping a target\u2019s time flow with their beauty or holding their image in place for a second so they get around of invisibility while their image is attacked instead. Immortality charm would be sucking the youth out of targets.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Stamina : Focuses on living til tomorrow; it\u2019s about survival by any means possible. Charm concepts include jumping into the future to a safer point, committing essence to bank healing time to gain instantaneous healing in combat and manipulating the traits of pregnancies they\u2019re involved with. Immortality charm would give them infinite life and damage no long does health levels, but ages them instead; additionally if I drop Immortality charms, then this is where most of the ways for Temporals to extend their life, as well as those of their allies.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Perception: Focuses on perceiving the tomorrow so the Temporal can plan accordingly. Sample charms include picking which path is the best for reaching their Quest, Creating a time loop to test the next essence rounds of potential actions, seeing the future potential in humans. Immortality charm would allow them to see the Destiny of others and slip into it, extending their life as long as they follow the path set down by destiny.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Manipulation: Focuses on planning tomorrow; was a key part of the Hourglass Conclave\u2019s apparatus as it allowed them to set up safe houses, followers and supplies in advance and often under the noses of the Deliberative. Charm concepts include convince fallen ghosts/mortals to reincarnate with a positive intimacy to the Temporal when they are slain, training mortals to be sleeper agents and making binding families to debts until the Temporal claims them. Immortality charm would they do something for a person and if they skip on some or all of the payment they get several extra years of life.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Extra Powers</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So the big question is (backwards) time travel possible for Temporals? I imagine jumping to the future to be relatively easy, but whether backwards trips are possible is the question. I see five potentials in order of my preference:</span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Only during Exaltation, that is the only time both Aion and Chronos allow time travel in order to facilitate their Exalts, otherwise it\u2019s impossible. Simple with no complications but little extra potential</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporals are the key to activating time travel through sorcery workings, artefacts or other powerful effects. Basically any time travel is a campaign defining event and a always a serious affair.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporals would have a charm that allows them to set a sort of saved point of history that they can rewind to; they can only time travel to that point and the further they go from it the longer it will be to recover from the jump. They would be able to take some allies (or captives with them) and recall all that happened in the previous time line. I can see this as being not too hard to implement and give the Storyteller a warning in advanced to any potential time travel shenanigans. Cost would be paid after the jump in temporarily reduced essence levels and willpower.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporals get backwards trips based on completing Quests \u2013 the bigger and more complicate a Quest the more points it gives for time travel to be divided between how far you want to travel in time, how far you can physically travel with the jump, number of people you can take and safety precautions when you jump (not being spotted, landing in a safe location, having warning of social complications, etc). Offers a solid result for completing quests in the largest boon of this version.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporals can regularly and easily perform time travel through charms. The distance through, if the jump is temporary or permanent, what they can do, how many people they take, etc are all determined by charm and the amount of essence they pay. When a Temporal time travels in this system they can change the past but face something called \u2018Continuum\u2019, a side-effect of fate that tries to force the timeline to remain as close as possible to the Temporal\u2019s timeline and is stronger the further back you go. So for example, if you fight a dragon blood in the evening and jump back in time to kill them before the fight, if you only jump back a day they wouldn\u2019t be replaced and you would not have to fight them later that day, if you kill them a week earlier, a member of their Wyld Hunt would fight you instead, and if you kill them a year earlier and entirely different dragon blood would have replaced them. That being said it also allows the Temporal to do various things if they interact with the past but try to flow with Continuum \u2013 kill the Dragon blood so his incompetent cousin takes his place on the Wyld Hunt for example, or use it to investigate the past or set up things that don\u2019t interfere with Continuum (like burying a pit trap under where the Dragon Blood will step). Offers the most freedom but also the most headaches for Storytellers with how much more freely they can toy with the past; however the Continuum does offer a constant pressure on the Temporals as history is drawn to remake their personal histories, creating plot hooks as the world shifts in ways they may not want as it gets closer to the original timeline they tried to flee from.</span></li> </ol> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The other major ability is \u2018Quests\u2019; each Temporal is aligned to either Chronos or Aion, who assign various goals they want done for some grand scheme. Where either of them have long term plans or just one-ups manship is largely unknown, but they still desire Temporals to be their main agents in Creation; some Quests redefine whole kingdoms while others merely involve getting children to their granny\u2019s house, their scale is variable and purviews wide as it seems the Titan of Time has many interests and sows their schemes in many fields. However many of their charms are keyed into the Quests and all Temporals have an innate sense of direction to where the main portion of their current Quest is. Example charm effects include a Strength charm that deal aggravated damage to enemies associated with a Quest, an Appearance charm that make integrating yourself into a social group easier if it\u2019s directly related to a Quest and a Perception charm that allows you to find the quickest route to your Quest.<br /> <br /> Whenever a Temporal completes a Quest they are offered a new one (possibly from a choice of many, I\u2019m not sure on that front) in a vision from their particular patron. Fortunately Quests are paid for when completed (Autochthon wouldn\u2019t let the Titan of Time produce Exalts without free will so instead of mindless slaves the Temporals were made to be mercenaries), so I see three potentials for this:</span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">XP sources; Temporals gain extra XP from completing Quests like how other exalts get it from roleplay.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Each Quest has a number of dots based on difficulty; when it is completed these dots can be used as a resource to generate temporary merits or add extra dice to a roll, representing Chronos or Aion\u2019s minor influence on the world to pay back their chosen.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Tied to option 4 of the Time Travel options, the Temporal gets dots to spend on Time Travel every time they complete a Quest; the bigger and more complex the quest, the more points they get.</span></li> </ol> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Temporals can learn Celestial Sorcery, Ivory Circle Sorcery and gain Mastery in Martial Arts; however some Temporals are marked with a reversal of the Necromancy and Sorcery alignments if it is the will of Chronos or Aion when they are Exalted. They can also summon the 3<sup>rd</sup> and 2<sup>nd</sup> circle souls of the Titan of Time through sorcery like rituals if they have Occult of 5 or 3 respectively, with all the same restrictions of sorcerous demon summoning (except for having to know sorcery); the Deva cannot be bound by this summoning (as they were not bound by the surrender oaths of the Yozis and their demons) but are usually predisposed to helping a Temporal, even one severing the opposite fetch soul, as they sense a kinship to the Temporals and are often wily enough to turn events to their own personal goals.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Great Curse and Essence Fever</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">All Temporals suffer the Great Curse, Chronos brought them into the Primordial War on the side of the Incarnae, so they are all doomed even if only half of them were on the winning side. Temporals experience the curse either as unbelievable regret or obsession with their Quests, and would be heavily tied to their castes. It builds up when the Temporal fails on tasks or loses something major based on their own decision.<br /> <br /> Past Caste: Want to get revenge on enemies, Correct unfixable wrongs, repeat old Quests, cancel out the effects of prior Quests.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Present Caste: Indulge in momentary pleasures before they\u2019re gone, run from damage, not only abandon but do as much as possible to avoid a Quest, rush into solving their current Quest as quickly as possible without thought or precaution.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Future Caste: Become insanely over protective of loved ones, try to cause disasters to be in \u2018control\u2019 (when you\u2019re really not), manically obsessing over the grand plans of Chronos or Aion, attempting to perfect plan how to complete a Quest without interfering with your life.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Their Essence Fever is closely tied to their patron, with Aioni Temporals drawn to fight and test the other Exalted while Chronosi seek to undermine the Yozis and the old systems. They often don\u2019t understand it in such grandiose goals, but an Aion aligned Temporal might seek to fight the Realm to strike at the Dragon blooded, while her Chronos aligned ally is seeking to liberate their slaves and commoners. However all Temporals are drawn to each other and any others who travel through time (such as summoned demons), but whether this is for good or ill depends on the Temporal in question.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Example Exalts</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Nellens Jukya; Aioni Past; a scholar who after a life time in sorcerous research realised his arranged marriage to another patrician could have worked out if he had invested time into it. Aion offered him to go back to his pre-civil war youth with a Quest to study and record all the various aspects of romantic love.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Sifu Willow, daughter of Sifu Tortoise; Chronosi Past; a daughter of a martial arts sifu in the west, she was denied any training due to tradition; she trained herself in secret but could never quite perfect the secret techniques she knew were trained behind closed doors. She accepted Chronos\u2019 offer of Exaltation and used her years of training to force her way into being accepted into the dojo in exchange for except a Quest to fight a stop a potential student from leaving.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cleric Augu Menta; Aioni Present; a former priest to an ancestor cult, she became disillusioned with the rising power of the dead in her home timeline; Aion sent her back so she could Crusade against the dead and let the living live their lives free from the weight of the fallen. Her current Quest is to kill a particular Abyssal exalt.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Jack the lad; Chronosi Present; a party loving nomad whose original life was one of endless duty to family and farm he ended up hating after 80 years. Officially on a quest to turn a Getimian to the Sidereal side, he prefers to indulge and live his life to the full.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Eled Windcatcher; Aioni Future; a skill navigator and merchant who careful plans her expeditions and trips across the Scavenger lands. Her Exaltation sent her back only a day as she regretted not taking one precaution that ended up costing her a minor business deal. When not worrying about every little detail and mercantile scheme she is a formidable Temporal completing many quests for Aion, even if they are mostly just smuggling various people (usually other Temporals) or goods to odd locations.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Marru Yopa; Chronosi Future; If you ask him, Marru Yopa is a skilled astrologer of the Varang city of Kesil and always has been. In reality he jumped back in his full body rather than take over his past self to correct the disastrously botched horoscope that doomed him to a life of military service rather than being a noted astrologer. When Chronos revealed him the truth, Marru took the Primordial\u2019s offer by the horns and has used a combination of blackmail and appearance charms to find a place in Kesil\u2019s social elite as an outsider astrologer of some noted skill \u2013 his manipulation charms are used for personal goals to take over the city and his Quest to set up cults to Chronos.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Comments</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTableGrid_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">These guys are the ones I have the most on but there are still some issues:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I need a good sobriquet for all Temporals, I can\u2019t keep calling them Temporals. Maybe \u2018spies\u2019 or \u2018shadows\u2019, but I don\u2019t know.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I need to iron the potential and mechanics for time travel and Quests.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I need to pin down what kind of animas they have and if that effects their charm themes.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I'm aware Chronos being over thrown by Zeus is inspiration for the Primordial War, but I based the assignment of Chronos and Aion based on their namesakes' roles - the Chronos as the God of the cycle of time (so change and the rise of new powers) and Aion as God of time eternal (so eternal systems and immortal beings.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Not sure about the Immortality charms, I might drop the concept and instead give a branch of Stamina to life extension.</span></li> </ul></td> </tr> </table></div> \u200b<br /> As for Avatastics, yeah the Hedge good example of what a gauntlet is like - a messed up realm that has it's own logic and changes those who go in there.<br /> <br /> For Industrials I've recently being thinking of doing them as people who have been given immense power to understand the world but it makes them slightly mad; Exaltation is done via the transfer of special charged nanites made by another Industrial - who started the process is unknown and more worrying is where the power comes as it seems to grow and develop as the Exalt learns more and more of the world. This mystery is central to Industrials and their identity, costing many of them their life as they seek for this answer. All they know of their history was a Solar was the first recorded person to use the nanites to Exalt someone after claiming she created them (which many consider to be pure nonsense), and from their they have risen and fallen several times, usually in colleges under a more powerful exalts purview, trying to not only preserve the knowledge of their forbearers but also to expand upon it.<br /> <br /> The nanites are something all Industrial can innately produce, with the basic substance being what defines the new Exalts caste: Metal, Organics, Energy/Spirit/Essence, Psionic waves and Spacetime. When the Industrial produces the nanites they can either immediately inject them into a candidate or preserve them in some way for later use; either way they possess the ability to choose potential exalts and successors. When a person gets their nanites it pushes them during a 'zeroth' stage and if they can prove themselves after a while by completing the first stage of a Magnum Opus it will ignite and properly Exalt the host.<br /> <br /> Main special powers are 'Magnum Opus' and 'Artiface'. A Magnum Opus is a singular project that defines an Industrial's life, like the doctoral thesis of a phd student, and is a quest to shape and define the limits of Creation in some way - one might focus on allowing them to eventually learn and master sidereal martial arts, while others might seek to develop an entirely new element; but such wonders are often obscure even to the greatest minds and are hard if not impossible to replicate (but that's what Exalted is about); advancing on the Magnum Opus is necessary for an Industrial to rise between Circles and become stronger - basically they have a singular moment of pushing/testing their theory until they can get more out of it; for example a Zeroth-First circle transformation is making samples of a new element; First-Second is making stable sample on a large enough quantity to be usable by others; Second-third circle is making elementals and manses of your new element; when the Industrial dies their Element is harder to produce and maintain and the secret will probably be lost in the years to come. Artiface is like sorcerous workings but more easily replicated, requiring a commitment of essence and some resources to recreate; these are usually specialist tools the Industrial relies on and defines their fighting style and approach to problem solving, but also seem like mad cap inventions to most sorcerers and scholars (basically, it's mad science inventions). Their anima is also super sentai armour and massively adaptable based on what the Industrial needs or wants. However they do have a major weakness; Industrials have to pick have abilities each time they go up a circle and they can no-long learn charms of that ability any longer and get refunded for charms in those abilities; this represents their minds specialising over time as they focus on greater degrees of knowledge.<br /> <br /> Also still don't think the name is perfect but at least I have a reason now (it started as derogatory mockery that they where 'Industrially produced chosen' by a First Age Lunar. Although Experimentalists is a cool sobriquet for them, thanks for that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T08:00:23-07:00","id":1563060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1561441#post1561441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, sorry for the late reply; this has been a busy time with personal matters and running a game but I am currently typing out all for all three but I've only completed Temporals so I'll post that for now:</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, now i'm the one who lost a month with personal stuff, pleasant overall but also quite chaotic. Somehow only noticed your post today. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, let me throw some comments and thoughts.<br /> <br /> - Temporals: Honestly, mostly lost with them. The more i read, the more stream-of-consciousness &amp; inchoate as actual characters they feel. Drop it all for now, make ONE &quot;Chosen of Regret/Revisionist/Undoer&quot; (let's be blunt, trying to undo/remake some past event seems to be the linchpin/seed that defines them), make some charmset and unique tricks package, put him or her in a mixed circle with, then see how things pan out and how might all the lore, castes &amp; etc be squirelled into them as you go along with play.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Atavists: I'm probably biased on those ones, but between the Hedge &amp; its denizens, the hypothetical goddess of lunar eclipses and maybe Arilak (that secretly preserves a number of beasts that should be long extinct), we have a solid core between Lunars, Liminals &amp; Abyssals to toy nicely with.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Industrials: What if their world is some sort of Ur-collective dreamscape/virtual reality/MMO somehow connected to Autochtonia, possibly related to the mysterious Nullspace, the conceptual realm that exists only where Autochthon\u2019s dreams and nightmares spill out into the inchoate void of Elsewhere? That might explain A LOT of things....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-13-2026, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T16:41:39-07:00","id":1563352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1563060#post1563060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> - Temporals: Honestly, mostly lost with them. The more i read, the more stream-of-consciousness &amp; inchoate as actual characters they feel. Drop it all for now, make ONE &quot;Chosen of Regret/Revisionist/Undoer&quot; (let's be blunt, trying to undo/remake some past event seems to be the linchpin/seed that defines them), make some charmset and unique tricks package, put him or her in a mixed circle with, then see how things pan out and how might all the lore, castes &amp; etc be squirelled into them as you go along with play.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While it is how they are Exalted, I never intended regret to be the major theme; what makes you perceive them as being overly regret themed? Their powers deal with a range of time based effects and not just trying to get past regrets while their patron relationships is a series of spy conflicts between two inscrutable beings that perceive time very differently from even other Primordials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1563060#post1563060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Atavists: I'm probably biased on those ones, but between the Hedge &amp; its denizens, the hypothetical goddess of lunar eclipses and maybe Arilak (that secretly preserves a number of beasts that should be long extinct), we have a solid core between Lunars, Liminals &amp; Abyssals to toy nicely with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to get my thoughts altogether on these guys (not helped by some extra work and running an Exalted campaign - curse all these excessive charms), but I'm drawn to idea of giving a central theme of trial and testing; their patron (not sure who that is) made them to not only preserve the legacy of several pre-human races, but also to test if humanity (especially) was still strong and could be overthrown and replaced; although I'm worried that would make them a little too much like Beast from Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1563060#post1563060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> - Industrials: What if their world is some sort of Ur-collective dreamscape/virtual reality/MMO somehow connected to Autochtonia, possibly related to the mysterious Nullspace, the conceptual realm that exists only where Autochthon\u2019s dreams and nightmares spill out into the inchoate void of Elsewhere? That might explain A LOT of things....</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Might work, I was thinking that their original patron is unknown and they instead pass on their Exaltations through &quot;nanites&quot; (which included such things as twisting the coils of fate/space-time and psychic imprints in a mortal); the investigation of their original patron is a major plot hook for gms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-12T08:08:17-07:00","id":1563992,"title":"","content":"Have been having a really hard time getting things from mind to text rolling, but speaking of Temporals, perhaps <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wxN1T1uxQ2g\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>might be worth watching.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551806-ideas-for-fan-exalted-types-yay-or-nay?p=1563352#post1563352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it is how they are Exalted, I never intended regret to be the major theme; what makes you perceive them as being overly regret themed? Their powers deal with a range of time based effects and not just trying to get past regrets while their patron relationships is a series of spy conflicts between two inscrutable beings that perceive time very differently from even other Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;undo the past/world&quot; is in your own words &quot;how they are Exalted&quot;, it becomes hard to say &quot;regret/rewriting existence to their wishes&quot; is not a major theme. If you want to veer out of this, one needs to explore other sorts of time travel - Doctor Who, and to a certain degree the Back to the Future series of films (and cartoon) hinge considerably more in &quot;time as a place to explore/tour through&quot; than going into the &quot;fight the future/remake the past&quot; path of all too many one-shot films (where the protagonist all too frequently screws up far more than succeds).<br /> <br /> Doctor Who frequently goes into &quot;dealing with secret history, policing things so weird occult stuff or other time travelers do not break down the timeline&quot;, while in Back to the Future the protagonists (usually) change things more by accident than intent and then have some countdown to correct things before the mistake erase them from existence or worse.<br /> <br /> Anyway, not every time travel adventure HAS to be about &quot;<i>altering the flow of history as we know it</i>&quot; and more of that might be what Temporals &amp;/or their Patron(s) need.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, should their maker be a Primordial really? In previous editions the Unshaped also had subsidiary aspects though not in the same degree as the Yozis and the more i think about it, the more i feel like Aion-Chronos as you developed so far does not <i><b>need</b></i> to have all the &quot;souls with souls with servitor spirit races&quot; convoluted baggage of a Primoridal, fallen or not. Plus &quot;time travel/manipulation&quot; as a thing makes more sense as the purview of someone messing around with the building blocks to start things that were not meant to happen than foundational, so to speak. Maybe some Unshaped, Ishvara or more obscure &amp; mysterious being, like Ketu the ineflable, unknown power behind the Dream-Souled? Just some thoughts)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-12-2026, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-23T02:23:51-07:00","id":1564924,"title":"","content":"About the &quot;Mad Sciencexalted&quot; (Industrials is not the point, so we might as well drop it), of late i've come to realize there's an elephant in the room that we have been ignoring big time, somehow.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Deviant:_The_Renegades\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> game in particular. AFAIK, it seems to cover almost if not all bases the OP is trying to hit on this brand of Exalted.<br /> (Damn, &quot;Remade&quot; even sounds spot-on as a sobriquet for them)<br /> <br /> The more i think about it, the more it feels like a must read on stuff to mine, riff or diverge from and get a better hang of what one is actually looking for.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, Creation itself has a logic and natural laws of its own though the subject is not explored in a systematic way. The world has patterns and cycles that are built-in in its structure and while watched over by a unfathomable number of spirits, do not on principle require them to exist and work. The absence of a field deity or spirit of a certain plant does not drive crops fallow or result in extinction and ecological disaster.<br /> <br /> Seekers of knowledge - or cosmic/esoteric power through the use of such knowledge - are part and parcel of Creation too. What if &quot;Magnum Opus&quot; were THE Remade, an endless search of an uncountable number of thuamaturgists, sorcerers, cultists and mad savants for the hubristic grail of crafting their own exaltation/exigence? What if the &quot;dirty bomb exigents&quot; were a springboard for the search of a number of beings to reverse-engineer the secret workings of the miracle of the Incarnae, to understand the lens as a tool fan their own spark to new heights and perhaps cheat the fates into a self-carved path to apotheosis?<br /> <br /> What if the Remade, these Deviant/Aberrant exalts were the failures and prototypes of this Great Work of blasphemous savants among mortals, gods, ghosts &amp; other spirits <i>in Creation</i> instead of another world/realm of existence? Another layer of intrigue &amp; mysteries instead of another place, how does that sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-26-2026, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}